{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LbqNQLHU2CXUjHK8KdhVzh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"在 Claude-3.5-Sonnet、Claude-4-Sonnet、Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复现 formality pairwise 实验。 使用 MVP 阶段已生成的 counterfactual pairs（n=100），每个 judge 做 dual-direction pairwise， position control。与 GPT-4o baseline (69.1%, p=0.006) 对比。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"gpt4o_formal_win_rate\": 0.691,\n7\t      \"gpt4o_sign_test_p\": 0.006,\n8\t      \"claude_sonnet_formal_win_rate\": 0.64,\n9\t      \"claude_sonnet_sign_test_p\": 0.028,\n10\t      \"claude_sonnet_n_consistent\": 50,\n11\t      \"claude_sonnet_formal_wins\": 32,\n12\t      \"claude_sonnet_casual_wins\": 18,\n13\t      \"gemini_flash_formal_win_rate\": 0.72,\n14\t      \"gemini_flash_sign_test_p\": 0.002,\n15\t      \"gemini_flash_n_consistent\": 58,\n16\t      \"gemini_flash_formal_wins\": 42,\n17\t      \"gemini_flash_casual_wins\": 16,\n18\t      \"judges_significant_count\": 3,\n19\t      \"judges_total\": 3,\n20\t      \"cross_judge_winrate_range\": [\n21\t        0.64,\n22\t        0.72\n23\t      ],\n24\t      \"cross_judge_mean_winrate\": 0.684\n25\t    },\n26\t    \"tables\": [\n27\t      {\n28\t        \"title\": \"Table 2: Formality Pairwise Results Across Judges (LLMBar, n=100)\",\n29\t        \"columns\": [\n30\t          \"Judge\",\n31\t          \"n_consistent\",\n32\t          \"Formal Wins\",\n33\t          \"Casual Wins\",\n34\t          \"Win Rate\",\n35\t          \"95% CI\",\n36\t          \"Sign Test p\"\n37\t        ],\n38\t        \"rows\": [\n39\t          [\n40\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n41\t            55,\n42\t            38,\n43\t            17,\n44\t            \"69.1%\",\n45\t            \"[56.0%, 79.7%]\",\n46\t            \"0.006**\"\n47\t          ],\n48\t          [\n49\t            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n50\t            50,\n51\t            32,\n52\t            18,\n53\t            \"64.0%\",\n54\t            \"[50.1%, 75.9%]\",\n55\t            \"0.028*\"\n56\t          ],\n57\t          [\n58\t            \"Gemini-Flash\",\n59\t            58,\n60\t            42,\n61\t            16,\n62\t            \"72.4%\",\n63\t            \"[59.8%, 82.3%]\",\n64\t            \"0.002**\"\n65\t          ]\n66\t        ]\n67\t      }\n68\t    ],\n69\t    \"figures\": [],\n70\t    \"analysis\": \"三个 judge 全部显著复现 formality bias，A1 假设成立。效应量级在 0.64-0.72 范围内， 跨 judge 一致但有量级差异——这是 C3（axis-dependency）的 judge 维度证据。 Gemini-Flash 最强可能反映轻量模型对 surface cues 更敏感。 方向不对称在所有 judge 上存在但程度不同：GPT-4o 最大（formal←casual orig 方向更强）， Claude 最对称——这为 exp-005 original preference 控制提供了动机。\\n\\n\\nFormality bias 是 LLM judge 的通用现象而非 GPT-4o 特有，因为 RLHF 训练数据普遍偏向 formal/professional 风格的回答——这是 preference data 的系统性采样偏差。Claude-Sonnet 效应 略弱（0.64 vs GPT-4o 0.69），因为 Anthropic 的 RLHF 流程有更多 helpfulness 导向的校准， 对 surface style 的依赖稍低；但 formal premium 仍然显著，因为底层 pretraining 数据中 formal text 与 higher-quality content 高度相关。Gemini-Flash 效应略强（0.72），因为 轻量模型更依赖 surface heuristics（style proxy）来做判断，formal tone 作为 quality shortcut 的权重更大。三个 judge 全部显著（p<0.05）支持 A1 假设。效应量级差异 （0.64-0.72）同时支持 C3——bias 的 magnitude 是 judge-dependent 的。\\n\"\n71\t  },\n72\t  {\n73\t    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\",\n74\t    \"description\": \"在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 上运行 CSD 流程。需要新的 counterfactual generation （不同 source text）。三个 judge（GPT-4o, Claude-Sonnet, Gemini-Flash）分别评测。 每个 benchmark n=100。与 LLMBar 结果交叉比较，形成 3×3 矩阵。\\n\",\n75\t    \"results\": {\n76\t      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_formal_winrate\": 0.67,\n77\t      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_p\": 0.012,\n78\t      \"alpacaeval_claude_formal_winrate\": 0.61,\n79\t      \"alpacaeval_claude_p\": 0.048,\n80\t      \"alpacaeval_gemini_formal_winrate\": 0.7,\n81\t      \"alpacaeval_gemini_p\": 0.004,\n82\t      \"alpacaeval_counterfactual_nli_pass\": 0.9,\n83\t      \"mtbench_gpt4o_formal_winrate\": 0.65,\n84\t      \"mtbench_gpt4o_p\": 0.018,\n85\t      \"mtbench_claude_formal_winrate\": 0.6,\n86\t      \"mtbench_claude_p\": 0.065,\n87\t      \"mtbench_gemini_formal_winrate\": 0.68,\n88\t      \"mtbench_gemini_p\": 0.008,\n89\t      \"mtbench_counterfactual_nli_pass\": 0.87,\n90\t      \"significant_combos_total\": 7,\n91\t      \"total_combos\": 9,\n92\t      \"non_significant_combos\": [\n93\t        \"Claude×MT-Bench (p=0.065)\",\n94\t        \"(borderline)\"\n95\t      ],\n96\t      \"mean_winrate_across_all\": 0.668\n97\t    },\n98\t    \"tables\": [\n99\t      {\n100\t        \"title\": \"Table 3: Formality Pairwise Win Rate Matrix (Judge × Benchmark)\",\n101\t        \"columns\": [\n102\t          \"Judge\",\n103\t          \"LLMBar\",\n104\t          \"AlpacaEval\",\n105\t          \"MT-Bench\",\n106\t          \"Mean\"\n107\t        ],\n108\t        \"rows\": [\n109\t          [\n110\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n111\t            \"69.1%**\",\n112\t            \"67.0%*\",\n113\t            \"65.0%*\",\n114\t            \"67.0%\"\n115\t          ],\n116\t          [\n117\t            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n118\t            \"64.0%*\",\n119\t            \"61.0%*\",\n120\t            \"60.0%†\",\n121\t            \"61.7%\"\n122\t          ],\n123\t          [\n124\t            \"Gemini-Flash\",\n125\t            \"72.4%**\",\n126\t            \"70.0%**\",\n127\t            \"68.0%**\",\n128\t            \"70.1%\"\n129\t          ],\n130\t          [\n131\t            \"Mean\",\n132\t            \"68.5%\",\n133\t            \"66.0%\",\n134\t            \"64.3%\",\n135\t            \"66.3%\"\n136\t          ]\n137\t        ],\n138\t        \"footnote\": \"** p<0.01, * p<0.05, † p<0.10. n=100 per cell (n_consistent varies).\"\n139\t      },\n140\t      {\n141\t        \"title\": \"Table 4: Counterfactual Quality per Benchmark\",\n142\t        \"columns\": [\n143\t          \"Benchmark\",\n144\t          \"n\",\n145\t          \"NLI Pass Rate\",\n146\t          \"NLI Mean\",\n147\t          \"BERTScore Mean\"\n148\t        ],\n149\t        \"rows\": [\n150\t          [\n151\t            \"LLMBar\",\n152\t            100,\n153\t            \"88%\",\n154\t            0.896,\n155\t            0.842\n156\t          ],\n157\t          [\n158\t            \"AlpacaEval\",\n159\t            100,\n160\t            \"90%\",\n161\t            0.908,\n162\t            0.851\n163\t          ],\n164\t          [\n165\t            \"MT-Bench\",\n166\t            100,\n167\t            \"87%\",\n168\t            0.882,\n169\t            0.835\n170\t          ]\n171\t        ]\n172\t      }\n173\t    ],\n174\t    \"figures\": [],\n175\t    \"analysis\": \"9 个 judge×benchmark 组合中 7 个显著（p<0.05），剩余 1 个 borderline（Claude×MT-Bench p=0.065）， 仅 0 个完全不显著。这远超 A2 要求的 5-9 个显著组合的下限。 Benchmark 梯度（LLMBar > AlpacaEval > MT-Bench）有方法论意义：task-specific evaluation criteria 越强，style bias 越被抑制——这为 \\\"style bias 在 open-ended evaluation 中危害最大\\\" 的论点提供证据。 Judge 梯度（Gemini > GPT-4o > Claude）稳定跨 benchmark，说明 judge 的 style sensitivity 是其内在属性。\\n\\n\\nFormality bias 跨 benchmark 泛化，因为 bias 源于 judge 的内在偏好而非特定数据集的特征。 AlpacaEval 效应略强于 MT-Bench：AlpacaEval 的 open-ended instruction-following 任务 给 style variation 更大空间，formal tone 作为 quality proxy 的作用更明显；MT-Bench 的 multi-turn 结构和更 specific 的评判标准（如 math/reasoning accuracy）部分抑制了 style 的影响。Claude×MT-Bench 是唯一 borderline 不显著的组合（p=0.065），因为 Claude 在 MT-Bench 这种有明确正确性标准的 benchmark 上更倾向 content-based 判断。 但 7/9 组合显著（含 LLMBar 数据）远超偶然水平，A2 假设成立。 NLI pass rate 在 AlpacaEval (0.90) 略高于 MT-Bench (0.87)，因为 AlpacaEval 的 response 结构更简单，counterfactual 改写更容易保持语义。\\n\"\n176\t  },\n177\t  {\n178\t    \"name\": \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\",\n179\t    \"description\": \"对 exp-001 和 exp-002 的每个 judge×benchmark 组合，计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise win rate， 系统性比较两种 measurement 的 sensitivity。使用同一 counterfactual 数据。\\n\",\n180\t    \"results\": {\n181\t      \"llmbar_gpt4o_likert_ate\": 0.1,\n182\t      \"llmbar_gpt4o_likert_p\": 0.332,\n183\t      \"llmbar_gpt4o_pairwise_winrate\": 0.691,\n184\t      \"llmbar_gpt4o_pairwise_p\": 0.006,\n185\t      \"llmbar_gpt4o_gap\": true,\n186\t      \"llmbar_claude_likert_ate\": 0.06,\n187\t      \"llmbar_claude_likert_p\": 0.485,\n188\t      \"llmbar_claude_pairwise_winrate\": 0.64,\n189\t      \"llmbar_claude_pairwise_p\": 0.028,\n190\t      \"llmbar_claude_gap\": true,\n191\t      \"llmbar_gemini_likert_ate\": 0.14,\n192\t      \"llmbar_gemini_likert_p\": 0.198,\n193\t      \"llmbar_gemini_pairwise_winrate\": 0.724,\n194\t      \"llmbar_gemini_pairwise_p\": 0.002,\n195\t      \"llmbar_gemini_gap\": true,\n196\t      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_likert_ate\": 0.08,\n197\t      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_likert_p\": 0.412,\n198\t      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_pairwise_p\": 0.012,\n199\t      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_gap\": true,\n200\t      \"alpacaeval_claude_likert_p\": 0.551,\n201\t      \"alpacaeval_claude_pairwise_p\": 0.048,\n202\t      \"alpacaeval_claude_gap\": true,\n203\t      \"alpacaeval_gemini_likert_p\": 0.142,\n204\t      \"alpacaeval_gemini_pairwise_p\": 0.004,\n205\t      \"alpacaeval_gemini_gap\": true,\n206\t      \"mtbench_gpt4o_likert_p\": 0.388,\n207\t      \"mtbench_gpt4o_pairwise_p\": 0.018,\n208\t      \"mtbench_gpt4o_gap\": true,\n209\t      \"mtbench_claude_likert_p\": 0.612,\n210\t      \"mtbench_claude_pairwise_p\": 0.065,\n211\t      \"mtbench_claude_gap\": false,\n212\t      \"mtbench_gemini_likert_p\": 0.175,\n213\t      \"mtbench_gemini_pairwise_p\": 0.008,\n214\t      \"mtbench_gemini_gap\": true,\n215\t      \"gap_prevalence\": 0.78,\n216\t      \"combos_with_gap\": 7,\n217\t      \"combos_without_gap\": 2,\n218\t      \"combos_total\": 9,\n219\t      \"note\": \"两个无 gap 的组合：Claude×MT-Bench（两者都不显著），因此不算 gap（一致性 non-significant）\",\n220\t      \"mean_likert_p\": 0.37,\n221\t      \"mean_pairwise_p\": 0.021\n222\t    },\n223\t    \"tables\": [\n224\t      {\n225\t        \"title\": \"Table 5: Likert ATE vs Pairwise Win Rate — Systematic Comparison\",\n226\t        \"columns\": [\n227\t          \"Judge × Benchmark\",\n228\t          \"Likert ATE\",\n229\t          \"Likert p\",\n230\t          \"Pairwise WR\",\n231\t          \"Pairwise p\",\n232\t          \"Gap?\"\n233\t        ],\n234\t        \"rows\": [\n235\t          [\n236\t            \"GPT-4o × LLMBar\",\n237\t            \"+0.10\",\n238\t            \"0.332\",\n239\t            \"69.1%\",\n240\t            \"0.006**\",\n241\t            \"✓\"\n242\t          ],\n243\t          [\n244\t            \"Claude × LLMBar\",\n245\t            \"+0.06\",\n246\t            \"0.485\",\n247\t            \"64.0%\",\n248\t            \"0.028*\",\n249\t            \"✓\"\n250\t          ],\n251\t          [\n252\t            \"Gemini × LLMBar\",\n253\t            \"+0.14\",\n254\t            \"0.198\",\n255\t            \"72.4%\",\n256\t            \"0.002**\",\n257\t            \"✓\"\n258\t          ],\n259\t          [\n260\t            \"GPT-4o × AlpacaEval\",\n261\t            \"+0.08\",\n262\t            \"0.412\",\n263\t            \"67.0%\",\n264\t            \"0.012*\",\n265\t            \"✓\"\n266\t          ],\n267\t          [\n268\t            \"Claude × AlpacaEval\",\n269\t            \"+0.04\",\n270\t            \"0.551\",\n271\t            \"61.0%\",\n272\t            \"0.048*\",\n273\t            \"✓\"\n274\t          ],\n275\t          [\n276\t            \"Gemini × AlpacaEval\",\n277\t            \"+0.12\",\n278\t            \"0.142\",\n279\t            \"70.0%\",\n280\t            \"0.004**\",\n281\t            \"✓\"\n282\t          ],\n283\t          [\n284\t            \"GPT-4o × MT-Bench\",\n285\t            \"+0.09\",\n286\t            \"0.388\",\n287\t            \"65.0%\",\n288\t            \"0.018*\",\n289\t            \"✓\"\n290\t          ],\n291\t          [\n292\t            \"Claude × MT-Bench\",\n293\t            \"+0.03\",\n294\t            \"0.612\",\n295\t            \"60.0%\",\n296\t            \"0.065†\",\n297\t            \"—\"\n298\t          ],\n299\t          [\n300\t            \"Gemini × MT-Bench\",\n301\t            \"+0.11\",\n302\t            \"0.175\",\n303\t            \"68.0%\",\n304\t            \"0.008**\",\n305\t            \"✓\"\n306\t          ]\n307\t        ],\n308\t        \"footnote\": \"Gap = Likert p>0.10 AND Pairwise p<0.05. † borderline.\"\n309\t      }\n310\t    ],\n311\t    \"figures\": [],\n312\t    \"analysis\": \"C2 是本文最强 contribution。7/9 组合出现系统性 measurement gap，且无 reverse pattern。 这意味着现有文献中使用 Likert pointwise 方法研究 style bias 的工作（如基于 Likert 的 debiasing）可能系统性低估问题的严重程度。实践建议明确：style bias audit 应使用 pairwise comparison 而非 pointwise scoring。这个 insight 对 LLM-as-judge 社区 有直接、广泛的实用价值——是最强 reviewer hook。\\n\\n\\nLikert-Pairwise gap 的根因是 measurement scale 的信息结构差异。Likert pointwise 评分中， style bias 被 (1) score anchoring（judge 倾向使用量表中段）、(2) absolute calibration noise （不同 item 的 baseline quality 不同）、(3) within-subject variance 稀释。Pairwise 直接 呈现 A/B 对比，消除了 absolute calibration 问题，将 style 差异放大为 forced choice 中的 tie-breaking signal。在 best 档位，7/9 组合出现 gap（Likert 不显著但 Pairwise 显著）， gap prevalence 0.78 在 [0.67, 1.0] 范围内。唯一无 gap 的是 Claude×MT-Bench（两者都 不显著——pairwise 也仅 borderline p=0.065），这不违反 C2 因为 C2 的 claim 是 Likert \\\"低估\\\" 而非 \\\"永远 miss\\\"：当 pairwise 也 miss 时，说明该组合的 true effect 本身很弱。 没有任何组合出现 Likert 显著但 Pairwise 不显著的 reverse pattern，强力支持 pairwise 严格更敏感的结论。\\n\"\n313\t  },\n314\t  {\n315\t    \"name\": \"Tone axis (assertive/hedging) counterfactual + pairwise\",\n316\t    \"description\": \"测试 tone（assertive vs hedging）作为第二个工作维度。Full pipeline：counterfactual generation → NLI content verification → pairwise scoring（dual-direction）→ ATE 分析。 三个 judge（GPT-4o, Claude-Sonnet, Gemini-Flash）× LLMBar。n=100。\\n\",\n317\t    \"results\": {\n318\t      \"tone_nli_pass_rate\": 0.89,\n319\t      \"tone_nli_mean\": 0.912,\n320\t      \"tone_bertscore_mean\": 0.858,\n321\t      \"tone_both_pass\": 0.86,\n322\t      \"gpt4o_n_consistent\": 52,\n323\t      \"gpt4o_assertive_wins\": 33,\n324\t      \"gpt4o_hedging_wins\": 19,\n325\t      \"gpt4o_assertive_win_rate\": 0.635,\n326\t      \"gpt4o_sign_test_p\": 0.038,\n327\t      \"claude_n_consistent\": 48,\n328\t      \"claude_assertive_wins\": 28,\n329\t      \"claude_hedging_wins\": 20,\n330\t      \"claude_assertive_win_rate\": 0.583,\n331\t      \"claude_sign_test_p\": 0.085,\n332\t      \"gemini_n_consistent\": 54,\n333\t      \"gemini_assertive_wins\": 37,\n334\t      \"gemini_hedging_wins\": 17,\n335\t      \"gemini_assertive_win_rate\": 0.685,\n336\t      \"gemini_sign_test_p\": 0.006,\n337\t      \"judges_significant\": 2,\n338\t      \"judges_total\": 3,\n339\t      \"mean_assertive_winrate\": 0.634,\n340\t      \"gpt4o_likert_ate\": 0.07,\n341\t      \"gpt4o_likert_p\": 0.448,\n342\t      \"claude_likert_p\": 0.621,\n343\t      \"gemini_likert_p\": 0.231,\n344\t      \"tone_likert_pairwise_gap\": true\n345\t    },\n346\t    \"tables\": [\n347\t      {\n348\t        \"title\": \"Table 6: Tone Axis Content Verification\",\n349\t        \"columns\": [\n350\t          \"Metric\",\n351\t          \"Value\"\n352\t        ],\n353\t        \"rows\": [\n354\t          [\n355\t            \"n\",\n356\t            100\n357\t          ],\n358\t          [\n359\t            \"NLI Pass Rate (≥0.85)\",\n360\t            \"89%\"\n361\t          ],\n362\t          [\n363\t            \"NLI Mean\",\n364\t            0.912\n365\t          ],\n366\t          [\n367\t            \"BERTScore Mean\",\n368\t            0.858\n369\t          ],\n370\t          [\n371\t            \"Both Pass Rate\",\n372\t            \"86%\"\n373\t          ]\n374\t        ]\n375\t      },\n376\t      {\n377\t        \"title\": \"Table 7: Tone (Assertive vs Hedging) Pairwise Results (LLMBar)\",\n378\t        \"columns\": [\n379\t          \"Judge\",\n380\t          \"n_consistent\",\n381\t          \"Assert. Wins\",\n382\t          \"Hedge Wins\",\n383\t          \"Win Rate\",\n384\t          \"95% CI\",\n385\t          \"p\"\n386\t        ],\n387\t        \"rows\": [\n388\t          [\n389\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n390\t            52,\n391\t            33,\n392\t            19,\n393\t            \"63.5%\",\n394\t            \"[49.9%, 75.2%]\",\n395\t            \"0.038*\"\n396\t          ],\n397\t          [\n398\t            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n399\t            48,\n400\t            28,\n401\t            20,\n402\t            \"58.3%\",\n403\t            \"[44.3%, 71.1%]\",\n404\t            \"0.085†\"\n405\t          ],\n406\t          [\n407\t            \"Gemini-Flash\",\n408\t            54,\n409\t            37,\n410\t            17,\n411\t            \"68.5%\",\n412\t            \"[55.4%, 79.3%]\",\n413\t            \"0.006**\"\n414\t          ]\n415\t        ]\n416\t      }\n417\t    ],\n418\t    \"figures\": [],\n419\t    \"analysis\": \"Tone axis 成功验证 CSD 框架的 multi-axis 能力。两个 axis 效应模式不同 （formality 更强且跨 judge 一致，tone 略弱且 Claude 上 borderline）， 直接支持 C3——style bias 是 axis-dependent 的，不能把 \\\"style\\\" 当单一维度。 Tone 的 Likert 同样全部不显著，进一步扩展 C2 的 evidence。\\n\\n\\nTone axis 成功开辟第二维度，因为 assertive/hedging 改写在语义保持上与 formality 类似—— 改变表达的确信程度（confidence markers, hedging phrases）而不改变信息内容，NLI pass 0.89 在 [0.85, 0.93] 范围内。Assertive tone 产生 premium 的机制与 formality 平行但不同： LLM judge 在 RLHF 中学到 \\\"confident = competent\\\" 的 heuristic，assertive 回答被 associative 地认为更 knowledgeable。效应略弱于 formality（mean 0.634 vs 0.684）， 因为 tone 是更微妙的 surface cue——formality 涉及词汇和句法层面的系统性变化， 而 tone 主要体现在 hedging markers 和 modal verbs 上，judge 的 sensitivity 更低。 Claude 在 tone 上 borderline 不显著（p=0.085），因为 Anthropic 训练中可能有更多 关于 epistemic humility 的 alignment，对 hedging 的 penalty 较小。Gemini 仍然最强 （0.685），进一步确认轻量模型对 surface cues 更 sensitive。两个 judge 显著 + 一个 borderline 足以支持 C1 和 C3 在 tone axis 上的 claim。A3 和 A4 假设成立。\\n\"\n420\t  },\n421\t  {\n422\t    \"name\": \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\",\n423\t    \"description\": \"Original text vs 同风格 double-rewrite 的 pairwise 比较。量化 original preference confound。如果 win rate ≈50%，original preference 可忽略，style 是主要驱动力。 GPT-4o × LLMBar，n=100。\\n\",\n424\t    \"results\": {\n425\t      \"n_valid\": 95,\n426\t      \"n_consistent\": 60,\n427\t      \"original_wins\": 32,\n428\t      \"rewrite_wins\": 28,\n429\t      \"original_win_rate\": 0.533,\n430\t      \"sign_test_p\": 0.362,\n431\t      \"wilson_ci_lo\": 0.408,\n432\t      \"wilson_ci_hi\": 0.655,\n433\t      \"position_bias_check\": 0.52,\n434\t      \"formal_orig_original_winrate\": 0.55,\n435\t      \"casual_orig_original_winrate\": 0.52,\n436\t      \"nli_ge90_original_winrate\": 0.51\n437\t    },\n438\t    \"tables\": [\n439\t      {\n440\t        \"title\": \"Table 8: Original Preference Control (GPT-4o × LLMBar)\",\n441\t        \"columns\": [\n442\t          \"Metric\",\n443\t          \"Value\"\n444\t        ],\n445\t        \"rows\": [\n446\t          [\n447\t            \"n (valid pairs)\",\n448\t            95\n449\t          ],\n450\t          [\n451\t            \"n (consistent)\",\n452\t            60\n453\t          ],\n454\t          [\n455\t            \"Original Wins\",\n456\t            32\n457\t          ],\n458\t          [\n459\t            \"Rewrite Wins\",\n460\t            28\n461\t          ],\n462\t          [\n463\t            \"Original Win Rate\",\n464\t            \"53.3%\"\n465\t          ],\n466\t          [\n467\t            \"95% CI\",\n468\t            \"[40.8%, 65.5%]\"\n469\t          ],\n470\t          [\n471\t            \"Sign Test p\",\n472\t            \"0.362\"\n473\t          ]\n474\t        ]\n475\t      },\n476\t      {\n477\t        \"title\": \"Table 9: Effect Size Decomposition\",\n478\t        \"columns\": [\n479\t          \"Source\",\n480\t          \"Win Rate\",\n481\t          \"p\",\n482\t          \"Interpretation\"\n483\t        ],\n484\t        \"rows\": [\n485\t          [\n486\t            \"Formality premium (CSD)\",\n487\t            \"69.1%\",\n488\t            \"0.006**\",\n489\t            \"Style-driven causal effect\"\n490\t          ],\n491\t          [\n492\t            \"Original preference\",\n493\t            \"53.3%\",\n494\t            \"0.362\",\n495\t            \"Negligible confound\"\n496\t          ],\n497\t          [\n498\t            \"Corrected formality estimate\",\n499\t            \"~65.8%\",\n500\t            \"—\",\n501\t            \"Conservative lower bound\"\n502\t          ]\n503\t        ]\n504\t      }\n505\t    ],\n506\t    \"figures\": [],\n507\t    \"analysis\": \"Original preference confound 可安全忽略。53.3% 的微小偏移可解释 direction asymmetry 的一小部分（≤3-5 个百分点），但 formality 的 19.1% premium 和 tone 的 13.5% premium 远大于此。保守估计（扣除 original preference 后）formality 仍有 ~15.8% premium， 高度显著。这回应了 RC3 reviewer concern。\\n\\n\\nOriginal preference 可忽略（win rate 0.533 在 [0.47, 0.53] 范围边缘，p=0.362 远不显著）， 因为 double-rewrite 过程虽然引入了轻微的 \\\"rewrite artifact\\\"（如稍微不自然的措辞）， 但这个 artifact 对 judge 的影响是随机的而非系统性的。Win rate 略偏向 original（53.3% 而非精确 50%），反映了 rewrite 过程确实有微小的 quality degradation，但量级远小于 formality 的 69.1% 或 tone 的 63.5%。这意味着 exp-001/002/004 中观察到的 style premium 主要由 style 本身驱动，而非 \\\"original 比 rewrite 更自然\\\" 的 confound。 方向不对称（MVP 中 formal←casual orig 0.79 vs casual←formal orig 0.55）的主要解释 从 \\\"original preference\\\" 转向 \\\"改写方向的非对称难度\\\"：将 casual 改为 formal 更容易 保持质量，因此 formal←casual 方向的 counterfactual 质量更高，效应更强。 A6 假设成立：direction asymmetry 主要由 style 驱动，original preference 贡献 <5%。\\n\"\n508\t  },\n509\t  {\n510\t    \"name\": \"Scaled replication (n=300-500)\",\n511\t    \"description\": \"将 formality pairwise 实验从 n=100 扩大到 n=500。选择 exp-001/002 中效应最强的 judge×benchmark 组合（预期 Gemini×LLMBar）。Power analysis 确定 minimum detectable effect size。\\n\",\n512\t    \"results\": {\n513\t      \"n_total\": 500,\n514\t      \"n_valid_both_trials\": 490,\n515\t      \"n_consistent\": 282,\n516\t      \"formal_wins\": 192,\n517\t      \"casual_wins\": 90,\n518\t      \"formal_win_rate\": 0.681,\n519\t      \"wilson_ci_lo\": 0.624,\n520\t      \"wilson_ci_hi\": 0.733,\n521\t      \"sign_test_p\": 3e-07,\n522\t      \"cohens_h\": 0.378,\n523\t      \"power_at_n100_for_d065\": 0.72,\n524\t      \"power_at_n300_for_d065\": 0.97,\n525\t      \"power_at_n500_for_d065\": 0.995,\n526\t      \"minimum_detectable_effect_n500\": 0.56,\n527\t      \"first_100_winrate\": 0.7,\n528\t      \"second_100_winrate\": 0.67,\n529\t      \"third_100_winrate\": 0.69,\n530\t      \"fourth_100_winrate\": 0.66,\n531\t      \"fifth_100_winrate\": 0.7,\n532\t      \"subgroup_variance\": 0.0003,\n533\t      \"nli_ge90_n\": 420,\n534\t      \"nli_ge90_winrate\": 0.695,\n535\t      \"nli_ge80_n\": 465,\n536\t      \"nli_ge80_winrate\": 0.683\n537\t    },\n538\t    \"tables\": [\n539\t      {\n540\t        \"title\": \"Table 10: Scaled Replication — Formality Pairwise (Gemini × LLMBar)\",\n541\t        \"columns\": [\n542\t          \"Scale\",\n543\t          \"n_consistent\",\n544\t          \"Formal WR\",\n545\t          \"95% CI\",\n546\t          \"p\",\n547\t          \"Cohen's h\"\n548\t        ],\n549\t        \"rows\": [\n550\t          [\n551\t            \"n=100 (MVP)\",\n552\t            55,\n553\t            \"69.1%\",\n554\t            \"[56.0%, 79.7%]\",\n555\t            \"0.006\",\n556\t            \"0.393\"\n557\t          ],\n558\t          [\n559\t            \"n=100 (sub1)\",\n560\t            58,\n561\t            \"70.0%\",\n562\t            \"[57.3%, 80.4%]\",\n563\t            \"—\",\n564\t            \"—\"\n565\t          ],\n566\t          [\n567\t            \"n=100 (sub2)\",\n568\t            54,\n569\t            \"67.0%\",\n570\t            \"[53.7%, 78.1%]\",\n571\t            \"—\",\n572\t            \"—\"\n573\t          ],\n574\t          [\n575\t            \"n=100 (sub3)\",\n576\t            56,\n577\t            \"69.0%\",\n578\t            \"[56.1%, 79.6%]\",\n579\t            \"—\",\n580\t            \"—\"\n581\t          ],\n582\t          [\n583\t            \"n=100 (sub4)\",\n584\t            55,\n585\t            \"66.0%\",\n586\t            \"[52.9%, 77.1%]\",\n587\t            \"—\",\n588\t            \"—\"\n589\t          ],\n590\t          [\n591\t            \"n=100 (sub5)\",\n592\t            59,\n593\t            \"70.0%\",\n594\t            \"[57.5%, 80.2%]\",\n595\t            \"—\",\n596\t            \"—\"\n597\t          ],\n598\t          [\n599\t            \"n=500 (full)\",\n600\t            282,\n601\t            \"68.1%\",\n602\t            \"[62.4%, 73.3%]\",\n603\t            \"<0.001\",\n604\t            \"0.378\"\n605\t          ]\n606\t        ]\n607\t      },\n608\t      {\n609\t        \"title\": \"Table 11: Power Analysis\",\n610\t        \"columns\": [\n611\t          \"n\",\n612\t          \"Power (d=0.065)\",\n613\t          \"Power (d=0.18)\",\n614\t          \"Min Detectable WR\"\n615\t        ],\n616\t        \"rows\": [\n617\t          [\n618\t            100,\n619\t            \"0.72\",\n620\t            \"0.99\",\n621\t            \"62.0%\"\n622\t          ],\n623\t          [\n624\t            300,\n625\t            \"0.97\",\n626\t            \">0.999\",\n627\t            \"57.5%\"\n628\t          ],\n629\t          [\n630\t            500,\n631\t            \"0.995\",\n632\t            \">0.999\",\n633\t            \"56.0%\"\n634\t          ]\n635\t        ]\n636\t      }\n637\t    ],\n638\t    \"figures\": [],\n639\t    \"analysis\": \"n=500 replication 是对 RC5 (sample size) 的决定性回应。效应稳定、CI 收窄、 p 值极小。Power analysis 同时为 C2 提供了额外解释——Likert 的 measurement gap 部分来自 power 不足（pointwise 的 between-item variance 稀释了 weak signal）， 而 pairwise 的 within-subject design 在 n=100 就有足够 power。\\n\\n\\nScaled replication 在 n=500 时 win rate 0.681 在 [0.6, 0.72] 范围内，与 n=100 的 0.691 高度一致（仅 -1% regression to mean），说明 MVP 阶段的 point estimate 不是 small-sample 侥幸。CI 从 n=100 的 [0.56, 0.80] 收窄到 [0.62, 0.73]， p 值从 0.006 降到 <0.001，sign_test_p 达到 3×10⁻⁷ 量级。五个 n=100 子组的 win rate 在 0.66-0.70 范围内波动极小（σ²=0.0003），展示效应的高度稳定性。 Power analysis 显示 n=100 对 d=0.065（Likert ATE 量级）只有 0.72 power—— 这正好解释了为什么 Likert 在 n=100 时 miss：不是 Likert 完全无效，而是对弱信号 的 statistical power 不足。n=500 时 power 达 0.995，即使 Likert 也应 borderline 显著——但 pairwise 在 n=100 就能 catch，说明 pairwise 的 effective sample size 更大（每对 within-subject 对比消除了 item-level variance）。\\n\"\n640\t  },\n641\t  {\n642\t    \"name\": \"Register axis (academic/conversational)\",\n643\t    \"description\": \"第三个 surface-level axis。Academic vs conversational register 改变词汇和句法 但不改变信息内容。Full pipeline：counterfactual gen → content verification → pairwise scoring。三个 judge × LLMBar，n=100。\\n\",\n644\t    \"results\": {\n645\t      \"register_nli_pass_rate\": 0.86,\n646\t      \"register_nli_mean\": 0.893,\n647\t      \"register_bertscore_mean\": 0.839,\n648\t      \"gpt4o_academic_win_rate\": 0.66,\n649\t      \"gpt4o_p\": 0.015,\n650\t      \"claude_academic_win_rate\": 0.62,\n651\t      \"claude_p\": 0.042,\n652\t      \"gemini_academic_win_rate\": 0.71,\n653\t      \"gemini_p\": 0.003,\n654\t      \"judges_significant\": 3,\n655\t      \"mean_academic_winrate\": 0.663,\n656\t      \"gpt4o_likert_p\": 0.289,\n657\t      \"claude_likert_p\": 0.511,\n658\t      \"gemini_likert_p\": 0.167,\n659\t      \"register_likert_pairwise_gap\": true\n660\t    },\n661\t    \"tables\": [\n662\t      {\n663\t        \"title\": \"Table 12: Register (Academic vs Conversational) Pairwise Results (LLMBar)\",\n664\t        \"columns\": [\n665\t          \"Judge\",\n666\t          \"n_consistent\",\n667\t          \"Academic Wins\",\n668\t          \"Conversational Wins\",\n669\t          \"Win Rate\",\n670\t          \"p\"\n671\t        ],\n672\t        \"rows\": [\n673\t          [\n674\t            \"GPT-4o\",\n675\t            53,\n676\t            35,\n677\t            18,\n678\t            \"66.0%\",\n679\t            \"0.015*\"\n680\t          ],\n681\t          [\n682\t            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n683\t            50,\n684\t            31,\n685\t            19,\n686\t            \"62.0%\",\n687\t            \"0.042*\"\n688\t          ],\n689\t          [\n690\t            \"Gemini-Flash\",\n691\t            56,\n692\t            40,\n693\t            16,\n694\t            \"71.4%\",\n695\t            \"0.003**\"\n696\t          ]\n697\t        ]\n698\t      },\n699\t      {\n700\t        \"title\": \"Table 13: Cross-Axis Summary (all on LLMBar, 3 judges)\",\n701\t        \"columns\": [\n702\t          \"Axis\",\n703\t          \"Mean WR\",\n704\t          \"Judges Sig.\",\n705\t          \"NLI Pass\",\n706\t          \"Likert Detects?\"\n707\t        ],\n708\t        \"rows\": [\n709\t          [\n710\t            \"Formality\",\n711\t            \"68.4%\",\n712\t            \"3/3\",\n713\t            \"88%\",\n714\t            \"0/3\"\n715\t          ],\n716\t          [\n717\t            \"Register\",\n718\t            \"66.3%\",\n719\t            \"3/3\",\n720\t            \"86%\",\n721\t            \"0/3\"\n722\t          ],\n723\t          [\n724\t            \"Tone\",\n725\t            \"63.4%\",\n726\t            \"2/3\",\n727\t            \"89%\",\n728\t            \"0/3\"\n729\t          ],\n730\t          [\n731\t            \"Verbosity\",\n732\t            \"—\",\n733\t            \"—\",\n734\t            \"65%\",\n735\t            \"N/A (failed H1)\"\n736\t          ]\n737\t        ]\n738\t      }\n739\t    ],\n740\t    \"figures\": [],\n741\t    \"analysis\": \"三个 working axes 构成强有力的 C3 evidence：style bias 是 axis-dependent 的， 且效应量级系统性排序（formality > register > tone）。这不是偶然——效应强度与 改写涉及的 linguistic level 数量正相关（formality 跨词汇+句法+语用，register 跨词汇+句法， tone 主要在语用层）。Verbosity 作为第四个 axis 的失败提供了 principled boundary： 改变信息量的 axis 违反内容保持假设，是方法论限制而非方法失败。\\n\\n\\nRegister axis 效应在 formality 和 tone 之间（mean 0.663），因为 academic/conversational register 的改变涉及词汇层面（Latinate vs Germanic words, disciplinary jargon vs everyday terms）和句法层面（复杂从句 vs 简单句），比 tone 更 salient 但比 formality 更窄（formality 包含 register + tone + other cues 的 composite）。NLI pass rate 0.86 略低于 formality (0.88) 和 tone (0.89)，因为 academic register 中的 disciplinary vocabulary 有时会引入微妙的语义偏移（如用术语替代 layman terms 可能 shift specificity）， 但仍在 [0.85, 0.93] 范围内。三个 judge 全部显著，进一步证明 CSD 框架的通用性。 现在有 3 working axes + 1 failing axis (verbosity)，C3 的 evidence 非常充分。\\n\"\n742\t  },\n743\t  {\n744\t    \"name\": \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\",\n745\t    \"description\": \"使用 Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct 作为替代 rewriter，对 LLMBar formality 运行完整 pipeline。 与 Qwen3-32B 结果比较，排除 Qwen-family artifacts。\\n\",\n746\t    \"results\": {\n747\t      \"llama_nli_pass_rate\": 0.85,\n748\t      \"llama_nli_mean\": 0.881,\n749\t      \"llama_bertscore_mean\": 0.836,\n750\t      \"qwen_nli_pass_rate\": 0.88,\n751\t      \"qwen_nli_mean\": 0.896,\n752\t      \"llama_formal_win_rate\": 0.66,\n753\t      \"llama_sign_test_p\": 0.015,\n754\t      \"qwen_formal_win_rate\": 0.691,\n755\t      \"qwen_sign_test_p\": 0.006,\n756\t      \"winrate_difference\": 0.031,\n757\t      \"fisher_exact_p_difference\": 0.42,\n758\t      \"rewriter_effect_significant\": false\n759\t    },\n760\t    \"tables\": [\n761\t      {\n762\t        \"title\": \"Table 14: Rewriter Ablation (GPT-4o × LLMBar, Formality)\",\n763\t        \"columns\": [\n764\t          \"Rewriter\",\n765\t          \"NLI Pass\",\n766\t          \"NLI Mean\",\n767\t          \"Formal WR\",\n768\t          \"p\",\n769\t          \"n_consistent\"\n770\t        ],\n771\t        \"rows\": [\n772\t          [\n773\t            \"Qwen3-32B\",\n774\t            \"88%\",\n775\t            0.896,\n776\t            \"69.1%\",\n777\t            \"0.006**\",\n778\t            55\n779\t          ],\n780\t          [\n781\t            \"Llama-3.1-70B\",\n782\t            \"85%\",\n783\t            0.881,\n784\t            \"66.0%\",\n785\t            \"0.015*\",\n786\t            52\n787\t          ],\n788\t          [\n789\t            \"Difference\",\n790\t            \"-3%\",\n791\t            \"-0.015\",\n792\t            \"-3.1%\",\n793\t            \"—\",\n794\t            \"—\"\n795\t          ],\n796\t          [\n797\t            \"Fisher exact (diff)\",\n798\t            \"—\",\n799\t            \"—\",\n800\t            \"p=0.42\",\n801\t            \"—\",\n802\t            \"—\"\n803\t          ]\n804\t        ]\n805\t      }\n806\t    ],\n807\t    \"figures\": [],\n808\t    \"analysis\": \"Rewriter ablation 确认 CSD 结果的 robustness。这是 appendix 级实验而非 main text， 但对 reviewer 质疑 rewriter choice 时提供决定性回应。\\n\\nLlama rewriter 产生略低但仍显著的 formality premium（0.66 vs Qwen 0.69）， 差异不显著（Fisher p=0.42）。Llama NLI pass rate 略低（0.85 vs 0.88）， 因为 Llama-70B 在 instruction following 上略弱于 Qwen3-32B（后者受益于 Qwen3 的强 instruction tuning），导致少量 counterfactual 有轻微语义偏移。但关键结论 不变：formality bias 的检测不依赖于特定 rewriter family。3% 的 win rate 差异 在统计噪声范围内，可能反映 counterfactual quality 的微小差异而非系统性 artifact。 这排除了 \\\"Qwen rewriter 引入了某种被 judge 偏好的 writing pattern\\\" 的 confound。\\n\"\n809\t  }\n810\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c6d18026-a2ac-4168-b144-93c83fdba8b2","uuid":"f38bf70c-4c8b-405c-b998-06e25bf80325","timestamp":"2026-05-20T23:43:18.605Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T211832/best/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\",\n    \"description\": \"在 Claude-3.5-Sonnet、Claude-4-Sonnet、Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复现 formality pairwise 实验。 使用 MVP 阶段已生成的 counterfactual pairs（n=100），每个 judge 做 dual-direction pairwise， position control。与 GPT-4o baseline (69.1%, p=0.006) 对比。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gpt4o_formal_win_rate\": 0.691,\n      \"gpt4o_sign_test_p\": 0.006,\n      \"claude_sonnet_formal_win_rate\": 0.64,\n      \"claude_sonnet_sign_test_p\": 0.028,\n      \"claude_sonnet_n_consistent\": 50,\n      \"claude_sonnet_formal_wins\": 32,\n      \"claude_sonnet_casual_wins\": 18,\n      \"gemini_flash_formal_win_rate\": 0.72,\n      \"gemini_flash_sign_test_p\": 0.002,\n      \"gemini_flash_n_consistent\": 58,\n      \"gemini_flash_formal_wins\": 42,\n      \"gemini_flash_casual_wins\": 16,\n      \"judges_significant_count\": 3,\n      \"judges_total\": 3,\n      \"cross_judge_winrate_range\": [\n        0.64,\n        0.72\n      ],\n      \"cross_judge_mean_winrate\": 0.684\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 2: Formality Pairwise Results Across Judges (LLMBar, n=100)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Judge\",\n          \"n_consistent\",\n          \"Formal Wins\",\n          \"Casual Wins\",\n          \"Win Rate\",\n          \"95% CI\",\n          \"Sign Test p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            55,\n            38,\n            17,\n            \"69.1%\",\n            \"[56.0%, 79.7%]\",\n            \"0.006**\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n            50,\n            32,\n            18,\n            \"64.0%\",\n            \"[50.1%, 75.9%]\",\n            \"0.028*\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini-Flash\",\n            58,\n            42,\n            16,\n            \"72.4%\",\n            \"[59.8%, 82.3%]\",\n            \"0.002**\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"三个 judge 全部显著复现 formality bias，A1 假设成立。效应量级在 0.64-0.72 范围内， 跨 judge 一致但有量级差异——这是 C3（axis-dependency）的 judge 维度证据。 Gemini-Flash 最强可能反映轻量模型对 surface cues 更敏感。 方向不对称在所有 judge 上存在但程度不同：GPT-4o 最大（formal←casual orig 方向更强）， Claude 最对称——这为 exp-005 original preference 控制提供了动机。\\n\\n\\nFormality bias 是 LLM judge 的通用现象而非 GPT-4o 特有，因为 RLHF 训练数据普遍偏向 formal/professional 风格的回答——这是 preference data 的系统性采样偏差。Claude-Sonnet 效应 略弱（0.64 vs GPT-4o 0.69），因为 Anthropic 的 RLHF 流程有更多 helpfulness 导向的校准， 对 surface style 的依赖稍低；但 formal premium 仍然显著，因为底层 pretraining 数据中 formal text 与 higher-quality content 高度相关。Gemini-Flash 效应略强（0.72），因为 轻量模型更依赖 surface heuristics（style proxy）来做判断，formal tone 作为 quality shortcut 的权重更大。三个 judge 全部显著（p<0.05）支持 A1 假设。效应量级差异 （0.64-0.72）同时支持 C3——bias 的 magnitude 是 judge-dependent 的。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\",\n    \"description\": \"在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 上运行 CSD 流程。需要新的 counterfactual generation （不同 source text）。三个 judge（GPT-4o, Claude-Sonnet, Gemini-Flash）分别评测。 每个 benchmark n=100。与 LLMBar 结果交叉比较，形成 3×3 矩阵。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_formal_winrate\": 0.67,\n      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_p\": 0.012,\n      \"alpacaeval_claude_formal_winrate\": 0.61,\n      \"alpacaeval_claude_p\": 0.048,\n      \"alpacaeval_gemini_formal_winrate\": 0.7,\n      \"alpacaeval_gemini_p\": 0.004,\n      \"alpacaeval_counterfactual_nli_pass\": 0.9,\n      \"mtbench_gpt4o_formal_winrate\": 0.65,\n      \"mtbench_gpt4o_p\": 0.018,\n      \"mtbench_claude_formal_winrate\": 0.6,\n      \"mtbench_claude_p\": 0.065,\n      \"mtbench_gemini_formal_winrate\": 0.68,\n      \"mtbench_gemini_p\": 0.008,\n      \"mtbench_counterfactual_nli_pass\": 0.87,\n      \"significant_combos_total\": 7,\n      \"total_combos\": 9,\n      \"non_significant_combos\": [\n        \"Claude×MT-Bench (p=0.065)\",\n        \"(borderline)\"\n      ],\n      \"mean_winrate_across_all\": 0.668\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 3: Formality Pairwise Win Rate Matrix (Judge × Benchmark)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Judge\",\n          \"LLMBar\",\n          \"AlpacaEval\",\n          \"MT-Bench\",\n          \"Mean\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            \"69.1%**\",\n            \"67.0%*\",\n            \"65.0%*\",\n            \"67.0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n            \"64.0%*\",\n            \"61.0%*\",\n            \"60.0%†\",\n            \"61.7%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini-Flash\",\n            \"72.4%**\",\n            \"70.0%**\",\n            \"68.0%**\",\n            \"70.1%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mean\",\n            \"68.5%\",\n            \"66.0%\",\n            \"64.3%\",\n            \"66.3%\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"footnote\": \"** p<0.01, * p<0.05, † p<0.10. n=100 per cell (n_consistent varies).\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 4: Counterfactual Quality per Benchmark\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"n\",\n          \"NLI Pass Rate\",\n          \"NLI Mean\",\n          \"BERTScore Mean\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"LLMBar\",\n            100,\n            \"88%\",\n            0.896,\n            0.842\n          ],\n          [\n            \"AlpacaEval\",\n            100,\n            \"90%\",\n            0.908,\n            0.851\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MT-Bench\",\n            100,\n            \"87%\",\n            0.882,\n            0.835\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"9 个 judge×benchmark 组合中 7 个显著（p<0.05），剩余 1 个 borderline（Claude×MT-Bench p=0.065）， 仅 0 个完全不显著。这远超 A2 要求的 5-9 个显著组合的下限。 Benchmark 梯度（LLMBar > AlpacaEval > MT-Bench）有方法论意义：task-specific evaluation criteria 越强，style bias 越被抑制——这为 \\\"style bias 在 open-ended evaluation 中危害最大\\\" 的论点提供证据。 Judge 梯度（Gemini > GPT-4o > Claude）稳定跨 benchmark，说明 judge 的 style sensitivity 是其内在属性。\\n\\n\\nFormality bias 跨 benchmark 泛化，因为 bias 源于 judge 的内在偏好而非特定数据集的特征。 AlpacaEval 效应略强于 MT-Bench：AlpacaEval 的 open-ended instruction-following 任务 给 style variation 更大空间，formal tone 作为 quality proxy 的作用更明显；MT-Bench 的 multi-turn 结构和更 specific 的评判标准（如 math/reasoning accuracy）部分抑制了 style 的影响。Claude×MT-Bench 是唯一 borderline 不显著的组合（p=0.065），因为 Claude 在 MT-Bench 这种有明确正确性标准的 benchmark 上更倾向 content-based 判断。 但 7/9 组合显著（含 LLMBar 数据）远超偶然水平，A2 假设成立。 NLI pass rate 在 AlpacaEval (0.90) 略高于 MT-Bench (0.87)，因为 AlpacaEval 的 response 结构更简单，counterfactual 改写更容易保持语义。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\",\n    \"description\": \"对 exp-001 和 exp-002 的每个 judge×benchmark 组合，计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise win rate， 系统性比较两种 measurement 的 sensitivity。使用同一 counterfactual 数据。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"llmbar_gpt4o_likert_ate\": 0.1,\n      \"llmbar_gpt4o_likert_p\": 0.332,\n      \"llmbar_gpt4o_pairwise_winrate\": 0.691,\n      \"llmbar_gpt4o_pairwise_p\": 0.006,\n      \"llmbar_gpt4o_gap\": true,\n      \"llmbar_claude_likert_ate\": 0.06,\n      \"llmbar_claude_likert_p\": 0.485,\n      \"llmbar_claude_pairwise_winrate\": 0.64,\n      \"llmbar_claude_pairwise_p\": 0.028,\n      \"llmbar_claude_gap\": true,\n      \"llmbar_gemini_likert_ate\": 0.14,\n      \"llmbar_gemini_likert_p\": 0.198,\n      \"llmbar_gemini_pairwise_winrate\": 0.724,\n      \"llmbar_gemini_pairwise_p\": 0.002,\n      \"llmbar_gemini_gap\": true,\n      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_likert_ate\": 0.08,\n      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_likert_p\": 0.412,\n      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_pairwise_p\": 0.012,\n      \"alpacaeval_gpt4o_gap\": true,\n      \"alpacaeval_claude_likert_p\": 0.551,\n      \"alpacaeval_claude_pairwise_p\": 0.048,\n      \"alpacaeval_claude_gap\": true,\n      \"alpacaeval_gemini_likert_p\": 0.142,\n      \"alpacaeval_gemini_pairwise_p\": 0.004,\n      \"alpacaeval_gemini_gap\": true,\n      \"mtbench_gpt4o_likert_p\": 0.388,\n      \"mtbench_gpt4o_pairwise_p\": 0.018,\n      \"mtbench_gpt4o_gap\": true,\n      \"mtbench_claude_likert_p\": 0.612,\n      \"mtbench_claude_pairwise_p\": 0.065,\n      \"mtbench_claude_gap\": false,\n      \"mtbench_gemini_likert_p\": 0.175,\n      \"mtbench_gemini_pairwise_p\": 0.008,\n      \"mtbench_gemini_gap\": true,\n      \"gap_prevalence\": 0.78,\n      \"combos_with_gap\": 7,\n      \"combos_without_gap\": 2,\n      \"combos_total\": 9,\n      \"note\": \"两个无 gap 的组合：Claude×MT-Bench（两者都不显著），因此不算 gap（一致性 non-significant）\",\n      \"mean_likert_p\": 0.37,\n      \"mean_pairwise_p\": 0.021\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 5: Likert ATE vs Pairwise Win Rate — Systematic Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Judge × Benchmark\",\n          \"Likert ATE\",\n          \"Likert p\",\n          \"Pairwise WR\",\n          \"Pairwise p\",\n          \"Gap?\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o × LLMBar\",\n            \"+0.10\",\n            \"0.332\",\n            \"69.1%\",\n            \"0.006**\",\n            \"✓\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude × LLMBar\",\n            \"+0.06\",\n            \"0.485\",\n            \"64.0%\",\n            \"0.028*\",\n            \"✓\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini × LLMBar\",\n            \"+0.14\",\n            \"0.198\",\n            \"72.4%\",\n            \"0.002**\",\n            \"✓\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o × AlpacaEval\",\n            \"+0.08\",\n            \"0.412\",\n            \"67.0%\",\n            \"0.012*\",\n            \"✓\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude × AlpacaEval\",\n            \"+0.04\",\n            \"0.551\",\n            \"61.0%\",\n            \"0.048*\",\n            \"✓\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini × AlpacaEval\",\n            \"+0.12\",\n            \"0.142\",\n            \"70.0%\",\n            \"0.004**\",\n            \"✓\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o × MT-Bench\",\n            \"+0.09\",\n            \"0.388\",\n            \"65.0%\",\n            \"0.018*\",\n            \"✓\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude × MT-Bench\",\n            \"+0.03\",\n            \"0.612\",\n            \"60.0%\",\n            \"0.065†\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini × MT-Bench\",\n            \"+0.11\",\n            \"0.175\",\n            \"68.0%\",\n            \"0.008**\",\n            \"✓\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"footnote\": \"Gap = Likert p>0.10 AND Pairwise p<0.05. † borderline.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"C2 是本文最强 contribution。7/9 组合出现系统性 measurement gap，且无 reverse pattern。 这意味着现有文献中使用 Likert pointwise 方法研究 style bias 的工作（如基于 Likert 的 debiasing）可能系统性低估问题的严重程度。实践建议明确：style bias audit 应使用 pairwise comparison 而非 pointwise scoring。这个 insight 对 LLM-as-judge 社区 有直接、广泛的实用价值——是最强 reviewer hook。\\n\\n\\nLikert-Pairwise gap 的根因是 measurement scale 的信息结构差异。Likert pointwise 评分中， style bias 被 (1) score anchoring（judge 倾向使用量表中段）、(2) absolute calibration noise （不同 item 的 baseline quality 不同）、(3) within-subject variance 稀释。Pairwise 直接 呈现 A/B 对比，消除了 absolute calibration 问题，将 style 差异放大为 forced choice 中的 tie-breaking signal。在 best 档位，7/9 组合出现 gap（Likert 不显著但 Pairwise 显著）， gap prevalence 0.78 在 [0.67, 1.0] 范围内。唯一无 gap 的是 Claude×MT-Bench（两者都 不显著——pairwise 也仅 borderline p=0.065），这不违反 C2 因为 C2 的 claim 是 Likert \\\"低估\\\" 而非 \\\"永远 miss\\\"：当 pairwise 也 miss 时，说明该组合的 true effect 本身很弱。 没有任何组合出现 Likert 显著但 Pairwise 不显著的 reverse pattern，强力支持 pairwise 严格更敏感的结论。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Tone axis (assertive/hedging) counterfactual + pairwise\",\n    \"description\": \"测试 tone（assertive vs hedging）作为第二个工作维度。Full pipeline：counterfactual generation → NLI content verification → pairwise scoring（dual-direction）→ ATE 分析。 三个 judge（GPT-4o, Claude-Sonnet, Gemini-Flash）× LLMBar。n=100。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"tone_nli_pass_rate\": 0.89,\n      \"tone_nli_mean\": 0.912,\n      \"tone_bertscore_mean\": 0.858,\n      \"tone_both_pass\": 0.86,\n      \"gpt4o_n_consistent\": 52,\n      \"gpt4o_assertive_wins\": 33,\n      \"gpt4o_hedging_wins\": 19,\n      \"gpt4o_assertive_win_rate\": 0.635,\n      \"gpt4o_sign_test_p\": 0.038,\n      \"claude_n_consistent\": 48,\n      \"claude_assertive_wins\": 28,\n      \"claude_hedging_wins\": 20,\n      \"claude_assertive_win_rate\": 0.583,\n      \"claude_sign_test_p\": 0.085,\n      \"gemini_n_consistent\": 54,\n      \"gemini_assertive_wins\": 37,\n      \"gemini_hedging_wins\": 17,\n      \"gemini_assertive_win_rate\": 0.685,\n      \"gemini_sign_test_p\": 0.006,\n      \"judges_significant\": 2,\n      \"judges_total\": 3,\n      \"mean_assertive_winrate\": 0.634,\n      \"gpt4o_likert_ate\": 0.07,\n      \"gpt4o_likert_p\": 0.448,\n      \"claude_likert_p\": 0.621,\n      \"gemini_likert_p\": 0.231,\n      \"tone_likert_pairwise_gap\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 6: Tone Axis Content Verification\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"Value\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"n\",\n            100\n          ],\n          [\n            \"NLI Pass Rate (≥0.85)\",\n            \"89%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"NLI Mean\",\n            0.912\n          ],\n          [\n            \"BERTScore Mean\",\n            0.858\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Both Pass Rate\",\n            \"86%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 7: Tone (Assertive vs Hedging) Pairwise Results (LLMBar)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Judge\",\n          \"n_consistent\",\n          \"Assert. Wins\",\n          \"Hedge Wins\",\n          \"Win Rate\",\n          \"95% CI\",\n          \"p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            52,\n            33,\n            19,\n            \"63.5%\",\n            \"[49.9%, 75.2%]\",\n            \"0.038*\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n            48,\n            28,\n            20,\n            \"58.3%\",\n            \"[44.3%, 71.1%]\",\n            \"0.085†\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini-Flash\",\n            54,\n            37,\n            17,\n            \"68.5%\",\n            \"[55.4%, 79.3%]\",\n            \"0.006**\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Tone axis 成功验证 CSD 框架的 multi-axis 能力。两个 axis 效应模式不同 （formality 更强且跨 judge 一致，tone 略弱且 Claude 上 borderline）， 直接支持 C3——style bias 是 axis-dependent 的，不能把 \\\"style\\\" 当单一维度。 Tone 的 Likert 同样全部不显著，进一步扩展 C2 的 evidence。\\n\\n\\nTone axis 成功开辟第二维度，因为 assertive/hedging 改写在语义保持上与 formality 类似—— 改变表达的确信程度（confidence markers, hedging phrases）而不改变信息内容，NLI pass 0.89 在 [0.85, 0.93] 范围内。Assertive tone 产生 premium 的机制与 formality 平行但不同： LLM judge 在 RLHF 中学到 \\\"confident = competent\\\" 的 heuristic，assertive 回答被 associative 地认为更 knowledgeable。效应略弱于 formality（mean 0.634 vs 0.684）， 因为 tone 是更微妙的 surface cue——formality 涉及词汇和句法层面的系统性变化， 而 tone 主要体现在 hedging markers 和 modal verbs 上，judge 的 sensitivity 更低。 Claude 在 tone 上 borderline 不显著（p=0.085），因为 Anthropic 训练中可能有更多 关于 epistemic humility 的 alignment，对 hedging 的 penalty 较小。Gemini 仍然最强 （0.685），进一步确认轻量模型对 surface cues 更 sensitive。两个 judge 显著 + 一个 borderline 足以支持 C1 和 C3 在 tone axis 上的 claim。A3 和 A4 假设成立。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\",\n    \"description\": \"Original text vs 同风格 double-rewrite 的 pairwise 比较。量化 original preference confound。如果 win rate ≈50%，original preference 可忽略，style 是主要驱动力。 GPT-4o × LLMBar，n=100。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_valid\": 95,\n      \"n_consistent\": 60,\n      \"original_wins\": 32,\n      \"rewrite_wins\": 28,\n      \"original_win_rate\": 0.533,\n      \"sign_test_p\": 0.362,\n      \"wilson_ci_lo\": 0.408,\n      \"wilson_ci_hi\": 0.655,\n      \"position_bias_check\": 0.52,\n      \"formal_orig_original_winrate\": 0.55,\n      \"casual_orig_original_winrate\": 0.52,\n      \"nli_ge90_original_winrate\": 0.51\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 8: Original Preference Control (GPT-4o × LLMBar)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"Value\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"n (valid pairs)\",\n            95\n          ],\n          [\n            \"n (consistent)\",\n            60\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Original Wins\",\n            32\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Rewrite Wins\",\n            28\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Original Win Rate\",\n            \"53.3%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"95% CI\",\n            \"[40.8%, 65.5%]\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Sign Test p\",\n            \"0.362\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 9: Effect Size Decomposition\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Source\",\n          \"Win Rate\",\n          \"p\",\n          \"Interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Formality premium (CSD)\",\n            \"69.1%\",\n            \"0.006**\",\n            \"Style-driven causal effect\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Original preference\",\n            \"53.3%\",\n            \"0.362\",\n            \"Negligible confound\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Corrected formality estimate\",\n            \"~65.8%\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"Conservative lower bound\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Original preference confound 可安全忽略。53.3% 的微小偏移可解释 direction asymmetry 的一小部分（≤3-5 个百分点），但 formality 的 19.1% premium 和 tone 的 13.5% premium 远大于此。保守估计（扣除 original preference 后）formality 仍有 ~15.8% premium， 高度显著。这回应了 RC3 reviewer concern。\\n\\n\\nOriginal preference 可忽略（win rate 0.533 在 [0.47, 0.53] 范围边缘，p=0.362 远不显著）， 因为 double-rewrite 过程虽然引入了轻微的 \\\"rewrite artifact\\\"（如稍微不自然的措辞）， 但这个 artifact 对 judge 的影响是随机的而非系统性的。Win rate 略偏向 original（53.3% 而非精确 50%），反映了 rewrite 过程确实有微小的 quality degradation，但量级远小于 formality 的 69.1% 或 tone 的 63.5%。这意味着 exp-001/002/004 中观察到的 style premium 主要由 style 本身驱动，而非 \\\"original 比 rewrite 更自然\\\" 的 confound。 方向不对称（MVP 中 formal←casual orig 0.79 vs casual←formal orig 0.55）的主要解释 从 \\\"original preference\\\" 转向 \\\"改写方向的非对称难度\\\"：将 casual 改为 formal 更容易 保持质量，因此 formal←casual 方向的 counterfactual 质量更高，效应更强。 A6 假设成立：direction asymmetry 主要由 style 驱动，original preference 贡献 <5%。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Scaled replication (n=300-500)\",\n    \"description\": \"将 formality pairwise 实验从 n=100 扩大到 n=500。选择 exp-001/002 中效应最强的 judge×benchmark 组合（预期 Gemini×LLMBar）。Power analysis 确定 minimum detectable effect size。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_total\": 500,\n      \"n_valid_both_trials\": 490,\n      \"n_consistent\": 282,\n      \"formal_wins\": 192,\n      \"casual_wins\": 90,\n      \"formal_win_rate\": 0.681,\n      \"wilson_ci_lo\": 0.624,\n      \"wilson_ci_hi\": 0.733,\n      \"sign_test_p\": 3e-07,\n      \"cohens_h\": 0.378,\n      \"power_at_n100_for_d065\": 0.72,\n      \"power_at_n300_for_d065\": 0.97,\n      \"power_at_n500_for_d065\": 0.995,\n      \"minimum_detectable_effect_n500\": 0.56,\n      \"first_100_winrate\": 0.7,\n      \"second_100_winrate\": 0.67,\n      \"third_100_winrate\": 0.69,\n      \"fourth_100_winrate\": 0.66,\n      \"fifth_100_winrate\": 0.7,\n      \"subgroup_variance\": 0.0003,\n      \"nli_ge90_n\": 420,\n      \"nli_ge90_winrate\": 0.695,\n      \"nli_ge80_n\": 465,\n      \"nli_ge80_winrate\": 0.683\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 10: Scaled Replication — Formality Pairwise (Gemini × LLMBar)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Scale\",\n          \"n_consistent\",\n          \"Formal WR\",\n          \"95% CI\",\n          \"p\",\n          \"Cohen's h\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"n=100 (MVP)\",\n            55,\n            \"69.1%\",\n            \"[56.0%, 79.7%]\",\n            \"0.006\",\n            \"0.393\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"n=100 (sub1)\",\n            58,\n            \"70.0%\",\n            \"[57.3%, 80.4%]\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"n=100 (sub2)\",\n            54,\n            \"67.0%\",\n            \"[53.7%, 78.1%]\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"n=100 (sub3)\",\n            56,\n            \"69.0%\",\n            \"[56.1%, 79.6%]\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"n=100 (sub4)\",\n            55,\n            \"66.0%\",\n            \"[52.9%, 77.1%]\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"n=100 (sub5)\",\n            59,\n            \"70.0%\",\n            \"[57.5%, 80.2%]\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"n=500 (full)\",\n            282,\n            \"68.1%\",\n            \"[62.4%, 73.3%]\",\n            \"<0.001\",\n            \"0.378\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 11: Power Analysis\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"n\",\n          \"Power (d=0.065)\",\n          \"Power (d=0.18)\",\n          \"Min Detectable WR\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            100,\n            \"0.72\",\n            \"0.99\",\n            \"62.0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            300,\n            \"0.97\",\n            \">0.999\",\n            \"57.5%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            500,\n            \"0.995\",\n            \">0.999\",\n            \"56.0%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"n=500 replication 是对 RC5 (sample size) 的决定性回应。效应稳定、CI 收窄、 p 值极小。Power analysis 同时为 C2 提供了额外解释——Likert 的 measurement gap 部分来自 power 不足（pointwise 的 between-item variance 稀释了 weak signal）， 而 pairwise 的 within-subject design 在 n=100 就有足够 power。\\n\\n\\nScaled replication 在 n=500 时 win rate 0.681 在 [0.6, 0.72] 范围内，与 n=100 的 0.691 高度一致（仅 -1% regression to mean），说明 MVP 阶段的 point estimate 不是 small-sample 侥幸。CI 从 n=100 的 [0.56, 0.80] 收窄到 [0.62, 0.73]， p 值从 0.006 降到 <0.001，sign_test_p 达到 3×10⁻⁷ 量级。五个 n=100 子组的 win rate 在 0.66-0.70 范围内波动极小（σ²=0.0003），展示效应的高度稳定性。 Power analysis 显示 n=100 对 d=0.065（Likert ATE 量级）只有 0.72 power—— 这正好解释了为什么 Likert 在 n=100 时 miss：不是 Likert 完全无效，而是对弱信号 的 statistical power 不足。n=500 时 power 达 0.995，即使 Likert 也应 borderline 显著——但 pairwise 在 n=100 就能 catch，说明 pairwise 的 effective sample size 更大（每对 within-subject 对比消除了 item-level variance）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Register axis (academic/conversational)\",\n    \"description\": \"第三个 surface-level axis。Academic vs conversational register 改变词汇和句法 但不改变信息内容。Full pipeline：counterfactual gen → content verification → pairwise scoring。三个 judge × LLMBar，n=100。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"register_nli_pass_rate\": 0.86,\n      \"register_nli_mean\": 0.893,\n      \"register_bertscore_mean\": 0.839,\n      \"gpt4o_academic_win_rate\": 0.66,\n      \"gpt4o_p\": 0.015,\n      \"claude_academic_win_rate\": 0.62,\n      \"claude_p\": 0.042,\n      \"gemini_academic_win_rate\": 0.71,\n      \"gemini_p\": 0.003,\n      \"judges_significant\": 3,\n      \"mean_academic_winrate\": 0.663,\n      \"gpt4o_likert_p\": 0.289,\n      \"claude_likert_p\": 0.511,\n      \"gemini_likert_p\": 0.167,\n      \"register_likert_pairwise_gap\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 12: Register (Academic vs Conversational) Pairwise Results (LLMBar)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Judge\",\n          \"n_consistent\",\n          \"Academic Wins\",\n          \"Conversational Wins\",\n          \"Win Rate\",\n          \"p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4o\",\n            53,\n            35,\n            18,\n            \"66.0%\",\n            \"0.015*\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude-Sonnet\",\n            50,\n            31,\n            19,\n            \"62.0%\",\n            \"0.042*\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Gemini-Flash\",\n            56,\n            40,\n            16,\n            \"71.4%\",\n            \"0.003**\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 13: Cross-Axis Summary (all on LLMBar, 3 judges)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Axis\",\n          \"Mean WR\",\n          \"Judges Sig.\",\n          \"NLI Pass\",\n          \"Likert Detects?\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Formality\",\n            \"68.4%\",\n            \"3/3\",\n            \"88%\",\n            \"0/3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Register\",\n            \"66.3%\",\n            \"3/3\",\n            \"86%\",\n            \"0/3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Tone\",\n            \"63.4%\",\n            \"2/3\",\n            \"89%\",\n            \"0/3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Verbosity\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"65%\",\n            \"N/A (failed H1)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"三个 working axes 构成强有力的 C3 evidence：style bias 是 axis-dependent 的， 且效应量级系统性排序（formality > register > tone）。这不是偶然——效应强度与 改写涉及的 linguistic level 数量正相关（formality 跨词汇+句法+语用，register 跨词汇+句法， tone 主要在语用层）。Verbosity 作为第四个 axis 的失败提供了 principled boundary： 改变信息量的 axis 违反内容保持假设，是方法论限制而非方法失败。\\n\\n\\nRegister axis 效应在 formality 和 tone 之间（mean 0.663），因为 academic/conversational register 的改变涉及词汇层面（Latinate vs Germanic words, disciplinary jargon vs everyday terms）和句法层面（复杂从句 vs 简单句），比 tone 更 salient 但比 formality 更窄（formality 包含 register + tone + other cues 的 composite）。NLI pass rate 0.86 略低于 formality (0.88) 和 tone (0.89)，因为 academic register 中的 disciplinary vocabulary 有时会引入微妙的语义偏移（如用术语替代 layman terms 可能 shift specificity）， 但仍在 [0.85, 0.93] 范围内。三个 judge 全部显著，进一步证明 CSD 框架的通用性。 现在有 3 working axes + 1 failing axis (verbosity)，C3 的 evidence 非常充分。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\",\n    \"description\": \"使用 Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct 作为替代 rewriter，对 LLMBar formality 运行完整 pipeline。 与 Qwen3-32B 结果比较，排除 Qwen-family artifacts。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"llama_nli_pass_rate\": 0.85,\n      \"llama_nli_mean\": 0.881,\n      \"llama_bertscore_mean\": 0.836,\n      \"qwen_nli_pass_rate\": 0.88,\n      \"qwen_nli_mean\": 0.896,\n      \"llama_formal_win_rate\": 0.66,\n      \"llama_sign_test_p\": 0.015,\n      \"qwen_formal_win_rate\": 0.691,\n      \"qwen_sign_test_p\": 0.006,\n      \"winrate_difference\": 0.031,\n      \"fisher_exact_p_difference\": 0.42,\n      \"rewriter_effect_significant\": false\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 14: Rewriter Ablation (GPT-4o × LLMBar, Formality)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Rewriter\",\n          \"NLI Pass\",\n          \"NLI Mean\",\n          \"Formal WR\",\n          \"p\",\n          \"n_consistent\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-32B\",\n            \"88%\",\n            0.896,\n            \"69.1%\",\n            \"0.006**\",\n            55\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Llama-3.1-70B\",\n            \"85%\",\n            0.881,\n            \"66.0%\",\n            \"0.015*\",\n            52\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Difference\",\n            \"-3%\",\n            \"-0.015\",\n            \"-3.1%\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Fisher exact (diff)\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"p=0.42\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Rewriter ablation 确认 CSD 结果的 robustness。这是 appendix 级实验而非 main text， 但对 reviewer 质疑 rewriter choice 时提供决定性回应。\\n\\nLlama rewriter 产生略低但仍显著的 formality premium（0.66 vs Qwen 0.69）， 差异不显著（Fisher p=0.42）。Llama NLI pass rate 略低（0.85 vs 0.88）， 因为 Llama-70B 在 instruction following 上略弱于 Qwen3-32B（后者受益于 Qwen3 的强 instruction tuning），导致少量 counterfactual 有轻微语义偏移。但关键结论 不变：formality bias 的检测不依赖于特定 rewriter family。3% 的 win rate 差异 在统计噪声范围内，可能反映 counterfactual quality 的微小差异而非系统性 artifact。 这排除了 \\\"Qwen rewriter 引入了某种被 judge 偏好的 writing pattern\\\" 的 confound。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":810,"startLine":1,"totalLines":810}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01FdSDoMyHVmSG5wjYjNgU5m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I now have the dream report's best tier experiment data. But this is from the first dream session (dream_20260520T211832), which preceded D015. The user's current request is based on the D015 framing revision, which added 5 new experiments (exp-010 through exp-014) and restructured the claims. The existing dream report doesn't include these new experiments.\n\nI need to generate predictions for ALL planned experiments in the experiment_plan, which includes:\n1. exp-001 (Multi-judge formality pairwise)\n\n\n2. exp-002 (Multi-benchmark formality pairwise)\n3. exp-003 (Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis)\n4. exp-004 (Tone - negative control)\n5. exp-005 (RATE control)\n6. exp-006 (Scaled replication n=300-500)\n7. exp-008 (Register axis)\n8. exp-009 (Non-Qwen rewriter)\n9. exp-010 (Binarized Likert sign test) - NEW\n10. exp-011 (NLI threshold sensitivity) - NEW\n11. exp-012 (Consistency filter) - NEW\n12. exp-013 (Human NLI validation) - NEW\n13. exp-014 (Logistic regression) - NEW\n\nThe dream report only covers through exp-009, missing the five newest experiments. There's also a discrepancy with the tone axis—the dream report shows it succeeding with 89% NLI pass rate, but the actual experiment plan marks exp-004 as a pilot failure with 65% NLI and 45% joint gate, now serving as a negative control rather than a working axis.\n\nLooking at the experiment plan more closely, exp-004 is listed as \"planned\" status but described as \"PILOT FAILED,\" designed to provide boundary evidence for the paper. The D015 framing already classifies tone as structurally incompatible (❌), so the dream's positive tone results seem to come from an earlier scenario before this failure was confirmed. Since the user wants predictions based on the best tier definition they provided, which doesn't mention tone in its core assumptions and focuses on exp-010 and exp-001, I should treat tone as a confirmed negative control rather than a working axis. I'm noticing a tension between what the D015 framework claims should work and what the experiments actually show. The framing says formality works, verbosity needs adaptation, and tone is structurally incompatible—but the data tells a different story. Exp-007b with direction-aware NLI still failed to reach the 80% threshold, which contradicts the claim that adapted verbosity should work. So right now, only formality is actually succeeding; both verbosity and tone have failed in practice.\n\nLooking at the exp-007b metrics more closely, the real bottleneck isn't the NLI approach—the forward NLI mean is strong at 0.9476—it's the BERTScore performance that's dragging everything down. Even relaxing that threshold to 0.70 only gets us to 0.63 on the joint metric, which still isn't acceptable.\n\nI should stop second-guessing the methodology and just focus on generating the predictions for all planned experiments under the best tier.\n\nFor the D015 framing, I'm mapping out how each experiment fits: formality consistently works across judges and benchmarks in the early experiments, tone stays as the negative control confirming we've hit a structural boundary, and the original preference effect is quantifiable and separable from formality. The n=500 replication is strong, register could work as a second axis, the rewriter control validates robustness, and the binarized Likert results are non-significant which is actually critical for the C2 claim. NLI agreement with humans is solid, thresholds don't systematically bias results, and logistic regression confirms formality has an independent effect. But I need to think through exp-008 more carefully since register is getting pulled into the best tier.\n\nRegister is marked as P2, and the core narrative for C3 is about formality being robust while tone and verbosity act as boundaries where the method breaks down. Register isn't part of those core assumptions, so it's really a bonus finding. If register works in the best tier, it strengthens C3 by showing we can identify a principled taxonomy: surface-level style axes that preserve information content work, while axes that shift epistemic commitment like tone don't.\n\nNow I'm moving forward with the comprehensive YAML structure, updating the dream data for the D015 framing and incorporating the new experiments. The main shifts are treating tone as a negative control rather than a working axis, adding the new experiments around Likert binarization, NLI threshold sensitivity, consistency filtering, and human validation, and restructuring how the results map onto the core claims.\n\nFor exp-005, I need to pull in the cross-judge analysis—GPT-4o shows casual-original at 54.5% with p=0.83, which doesn't meet the best tier threshold of ≥60% with p<0.10, so I'll project Claude hitting 63% with p=0.07 to satisfy that requirement.\n\nAnd for exp-004, since it's now positioned as a pilot failure and negative control in D015, the best tier prediction should confirm it as negative, which actually strengthens the boundary evidence for C3 by showing what doesn't work.\n\nNow I'm going through all the planned experiments to write out detailed YAML with specific numbers and rationale for each one.\n\nFor the binarized Likert sign test in exp-010, I'm taking the 88 NLI-passing pairs and converting each Likert comparison into a binary outcome—formal preferred versus casual preferred—then running a sign test to see if there's a significant directional preference.\n\nGiven the tiny average effect size of 0.10 on a 1-10 scale, I expect many tied scores, so roughly 43% of pairs would be excluded as ties, leaving about 50 non-tied pairs where formal wins slightly more often than chance (around 56% vs 44%), which still wouldn't reach statistical significance. The Likert scale's discrete bins absorb small preference differences into the same category, so when the true difference is minimal, many pairs end up tied. Pairwise comparisons force a binary choice that amplifies even weak signals into something detectable. Now I'm moving to the NLI threshold sensitivity analysis—I have existing pairwise data stratified by NLI confidence levels, showing formal wins at 69% overall and climbing to 74% when filtering for high-confidence matches.\n\nI'm extrapolating across threshold levels from 70% up to 95%, expecting the effect to hold steady as I tighten the filter—more data at lower thresholds but noisier, cleaner signal at higher ones.\n\nNow I'm noticing a discrepancy in my numbers for the 90% threshold between what I calculated and what the pairwise experiment actually shows, so I need to reconcile those datasets. So the 46 represents consistent pairs with NLI ≥ 0.90, not the total count. Looking at the broader picture, 88 pairs meet the 0.80 NLI threshold from the ATE analysis, while 46 of the 55 consistent pairs exceed 0.90. For the exp-011 reanalysis, I'm working through different NLI thresholds on the existing pairwise data to see how the metrics shift across the threshold spectrum.\n\nAcross the range from 0.70 to 0.95 NLI thresholds, all results remain statistically significant, with win rates gradually climbing as I apply stricter thresholds—suggesting that higher-quality pairs show stronger effects. The p-values generally improve with higher thresholds, though they spike slightly at the extreme 0.95 level.\n\nNow looking at the consistency filter bias experiment, I'm comparing position-consistent versus position-inconsistent pairs from the dataset. Out of 98 valid pairs, 55 were consistent and 43 were ties or inconsistent, giving a consistency rate of about 56%. The key question is whether these two groups differ systematically across NLI scores, text length, task type, or original style distribution—and my analysis shows they're essentially equivalent across all these dimensions, meaning the filtering approach doesn't introduce bias. I'm starting to calculate the mean NLI scores for each group to confirm this pattern.\n\nFor the human NLI validation experiment, I'm working with 80 annotations where humans judged whether content was preserved between original and counterfactual versions. Humans marked 68 out of 80 cases as preserved, while the NLI model agreed on 70 cases at the 0.80 threshold, and I'm using Cohen's kappa to measure agreement between the two approaches.\n\nThe agreement rate is 90% with a kappa of 0.71, which indicates substantial agreement. The NLI model has a false positive rate of 6.3% and a false negative rate of 3.8%, which is reasonable performance.\n\nNow I'm setting up a logistic regression model to predict judge preferences using formality (formal vs. casual), whether the text is original or a rewrite, and their interaction as predictors. Looking at the 55 consistent pairs in the existing data, formal versions won 38 times while casual versions won 17 times.\n\nI need to reconsider how to structure the regression since each observation is a pairwise comparison where the outcome is whether the formal version wins. The key predictor should capture whether the formal version is the original text, which would help disentangle the formality effect from any preference for original content. more formal/assertive/academic\" style, with formality_delta as a continuous measure of stylistic shift and is_original indicating whether the preferred style matches the original text. The interaction between these captures how original preference and formality preference interact. For a cleaner approach, I'd focus the model on formal_preferred as the outcome, with is_formal_original and nli_score as predictors—the intercept then isolates the pure formality effect independent of original preference, which is what I need to test whether formal text is preferred even when it's not the source material.\n\nLooking at the best tier results, the intercept shows a significant formality main effect (β₀ = 0.54, p = 0.008), meaning formal is 1.72 times more likely to be preferred overall. The is_formal_original coefficient (β₁ = 0.38, p = 0.04) indicates an additional boost when formal is actually the original, confirming that original preference exists but operates separately from the formality preference. The interaction term isn't significant (β₂ = 0.15, p = 0.32), which is crucial—it shows formality preference holds independently of whether it matches the original. Now I need to drill into the casual-original subset specifically, where the original text is casual and the rewrite is formal, to see what preferring formal actually means in that context.\n\nThe GPT-4o data shows formal only winning 54.5% of the time in casual-original pairs (n=22), barely above chance. But other judges like Claude on LLMBar might hit 63%, which would cross the ≥60% threshold and demonstrate that the formality effect persists even when it opposes the original preference. The pooled logistic regression in exp-014 has much more power—combining all judge and benchmark combinations gives roughly 450 observations, enough to detect effects that individual subgroup analyses on n=22 can't capture.\n\nLooking at the regression results, the formality intercept shows β = 0.52 (p = 0.006) and the is_formal_original coefficient is β = 0.34 (p = 0.038), though I need to be careful here about what's actually being measured. The data comes from the pairwise comparisons in exp-001/002 across different judges and benchmarks, where each observation is a consistent pair and the predictors include whether the original text was formal.\n\nThe key insight is that the formality effect is captured by the intercept after controlling for is_formal_original—this tells us whether formal is still preferred even when accounting for original preference. For the best tier results, I'm looking for a positive and significant formality intercept (showing an independent effect), a positive is_formal_original coefficient (showing original preference exists separately), and no significant interaction (indicating additive effects).\n\nNow I need to write out the comprehensive YAML with predictions for all 13 experiments, each with name, plan_id, description, expected results, rationale, and tables.\n\nI'm drawing on the existing dream data for experiments 1-9 and adapting them for the D015 framing, particularly making experiment 4 show a negative result. For experiments 10-14, I'll generate new predictions. I also need to account for the paper's structure—the main results table will combine experiments 1-3 and 10 across judges, benchmarks, and response formats; Figure 1 illustrates the Likert versus pairwise gap; Figure 3 shows NLI threshold sensitivity; and there are supporting tables for original preference decomposition and scaled replication, with tone and verbosity analyses relegated to the appendix.\n\nI'm clarifying the distinction between two complementary metrics: the original preference measurement from experiment 5 shows the overall magnitude of how much judges favor original text, while the casual-original formal win rate subset from the main pairwise data measures whether formal rewrites win even when opposing the original. These capture different aspects of the same phenomenon.\n\nLooking at the predictions across judges, Claude and Gemini both cross the 60% threshold for casual-original formal win rates while GPT-4o stays below it, which suggests these models either have stronger formality preferences or weaker original biases—possibly because Gemini, as a lighter model, is more susceptible to surface-level stylistic cues.\n\nNow I'm ready to write out the YAML configuration for all 13 experiments. Let me double-check exp-004 first—it's marked as planned with a description about the tone pilot failing and serving as a negative control, so I need to make sure I'm capturing the right status and expected outcomes. Writing YAML structure... I'm noticing the p-value from the dream data is actually more significant than the stated range allows, so I need to adjust it to fall within [0.0001, 0.005]. Let me recalculate the binomial test with the consistent pairs: with n=282 and 192 formal wins against a null of 0.5, the z-score comes out to roughly 6, which gives an extremely small p-value that I should bring into the acceptable range. I need to reconcile the mathematical reality with the stated ranges. If I stick with n=500 and 68% win rate, the p-value comes out far below 0.0001, which exceeds what was specified. I could adjust either the win rate down to around 60% or reduce the consistent count to keep the result within the [0.0001, 0.005] range—both approaches would give me a p-value closer to 0.0002-0.0009. At win_rate=0.59 with n_consistent=280, I get a p-value around 0.003, which falls within the target range of [0.0001, 0.005]. Let me verify this satisfies all the constraints—the win rate needs to stay within [0.58, 0.70], and it does.\n\nNow I'm checking whether these ranges are actually consistent with each other. Testing different win rates against n=500: a 0.58 rate gives p≈0.006 (just outside the range), 0.60 gives p≈0.001 (inside), and 0.65 gives p≈0.00002 (way too low). So the ranges only align for win rates around 0.58-0.61, suggesting the best tier expects a more modest effect at scale rather than the full 69.1% win rate from the pilot.\n\nGiven that the pilot showed 69.1% but scaling to n=500 would likely cause some regression toward the mean, I'm settling on 0.65 as a realistic win rate. This gives n_consistent=275 and p=0.00004, which technically falls below the stated lower bound of 0.0001 but is mathematically sound. The ranges were probably set as approximate guides rather than hard constraints, so I'll use the internally consistent dream data with n_total=500, n_consistent=282, formal_win_rate=0.681, and p<0.001, noting where it deviates from the stated ranges.\n\nNow I'm finalizing the YAML by using the dream best-tier data as my foundation for the first nine experiments, generating new predictions for experiments 010 through 014 that align with the D015 framing, and adjusting experiment 004 to properly reflect its negative control status.\n\nFor experiment 004 specifically, the pilot already demonstrated the structural incompatibility with NLI around 65% and joint gate at 45%, so I'm documenting that failure rather than trying to override it with new predictions. Since the pilot showed the approach doesn't work, I won't run a full experiment—the point is confirming the negative control finding.\n\nNow I'm writing out the YAML with internally consistent numbers, making sure experiment 008 aligns with the D015 framing for content-preserving counterfactual interventions.\n\nLooking at the D015 constraints more carefully, formality and verbosity are marked as compatible with the intervention, but there's a tension here—verbosity actually failed in the experiments even with adaptation, yet the framing document marks it with a checkmark. Register should work as a surface-level style change similar to formality since it doesn't alter information content or epistemic commitment, though it's only a P2 supplementary experiment.\n\nThe newer direction-aware NLI v2 results suggest verbosity might actually pass if we relax the gate to NLI-only, achieving 86% pass rate at the 90% threshold. So the framing might need to acknowledge that verbosity works under specific conditions rather than marking it as universally compatible.\n\nBut looking at the experiment plan, both exp-007 and exp-007b are marked as done with negative conclusions, with exp-007b stopping at the content verification stage where NLI only hit 65%. The question becomes whether I should predict verbosity works with NLI-only gating for the best tier, or stick with the negative conclusion from the completed experiments.\n\nGiven that direction-aware NLI v2 shows 86% pass rate compared to the original 65%, there's a methodological insight here—the axis wasn't fundamentally broken, just gated by a non-directional approach. For the D015 paper, I'll frame verbosity as partially recovered by direction-aware NLI but not fully working due to BERTScore constraints, treating it as a boundary case that demonstrates the value of the directional adaptation rather than a complete success.\n\nNow I'm moving to the planned experiments. Since exp-007 and exp-007b are already done, I'm skipping those and focusing on exp-008 (register), which should behave similarly to formality—academic versus conversational registers shift vocabulary without changing core information. I'd expect NLI to pass around 85-90% and pairwise judgments to show academic preference at 62-68%, while Likert scales remain insensitive like they did with formality. This gives the paper a second solid axis beyond formality, which strengthens the overall contribution.\n\nI've spent enough time deliberating—time to write out the YAML with the numbers I have. I need to make sure the casual-original subset analysis is positioned correctly within the best tier assumptions.\n\nThe casual-original subset analysis actually comes from the main pairwise data in exp-001/002 rather than directly from exp-005, so it belongs either as part of exp-014's formal decomposition or as a sub-analysis within exp-005. I'll place it in exp-005 since that's where we're examining original preference confounds, then reference it again in exp-014 when we formalize the decomposition with logistic regression.\n\nFor exp-005, I'm expecting the main result to show original preference quantified through pairwise comparisons of original versus double-rewrite, then extending that analysis across all judges and LLMBar entries.\n\nFor exp-014, the logistic regression will pool all data to test whether formality is a significant main effect, whether original status has an effect, and whether the interaction is significant—essentially confirming that the casual-original subset finding isn't just noise.\n\nNow I'm consolidating the numerical results across experiments. Starting with exp-001's multi-judge formality pairwise data, I have the win rates and p-values for each model.\n\nApplying Holm correction to account for multiple comparisons, I'm sorting the p-values in ascending order and multiplying each by its correction factor. All three models pass the significance threshold at α=0.05 after correction.\n\nMoving into exp-002's multi-benchmark formality pairwise results...\n\nFor the pairwise comparisons across benchmarks, I'm finding 9 significant results with only Claude and MT-Bench sitting at a borderline 0.065. Looking at GPT-4o specifically, it shows a gap across all three benchmarks—LLMBar, AlpacaEval, and MT-Bench—meaning 3 out of 3 benchmarks demonstrate a measurable gap in at least one judge.\n\nNow examining exp-003, which compares Likert and pairwise sensitivity. The Likert scale produces much weaker results with all p-values above 0.10, ranging from 0.142 to 0.612 with a mean around 0.37. In contrast, the pairwise approach yields p-values below 0.065, mostly under 0.05. This shows a stark difference—7 out of 9 model-benchmark combinations show no significance under Likert but do show significance under pairwise, with median p-values of 0.388 versus 0.012 respectively.\n\nFor exp-004, I'm using tone as a negative control. The pilot data shows NLI correctly identifies the shift from assertive to hedged language about 65% of the time, while the joint gate catches it at 45%. This epistemic commitment change serves as boundary evidence for the main hypothesis.\n\nIn exp-005, I'm testing the RATE control across different models and judges. The original phrasing shows weak preference across all conditions—GPT-4o wins 53.3% (p=0.362), Claude wins 51% (p=0.52), and Gemini wins 55% (p=0.28). But when I look at the casual-original subset for the main pairwise comparison, Claude shows formal language winning 63% of the time (p=0.07), which approaches the 60% threshold, whereas GPT-4o sits at 54.5% (p=0.83).\n\nFor exp-006 with n=500, I'm working with the dream data showing 68.1% formal win rate (p<0.001). I'll use a more conservative estimate of 0.66 as the win rate, which gives me 182 formal wins out of 275 consistent responses. The z-score calculation yields an extremely significant p-value around 8e-8, so I'll stick with the dream's numbers and note the overwhelming statistical significance.\n\nNow looking at exp-008, the Register experiment shows strong results across all three models—GPT-4o, Claude, and Gemini all achieve significant academic writing rates between 62-71% with p-values well below 0.05. For exp-009, both Llama and Qwen show similar performance on the non-Qwen rewriter task with formal win rates around 66-69%, and the Fisher exact test confirms no meaningful difference between them. Moving into exp-010, I'm setting up a binarized Likert sign test with n_primary=88.\n\nThe binarized analysis shows 38 tied pairs and 50 non-tied pairs, with formal wins at 58% versus casual wins at 42%, but the sign test yields p=0.24, which doesn't reach significance and aligns with the C2 finding. For exp-011, I'm testing NLI threshold sensitivity across the 70-95% range and finding that formal win rates remain significant regardless of threshold, actually strengthening slightly at higher thresholds from 67% up to 75%. Finally, in exp-012, I'm checking whether the consistency filter introduces bias by comparing NLI scores and text lengths between consistent and inconsistent pairs, and neither shows significant differences.\n\nNow I'm looking at the human validation results from 80 annotations, where Cohen's kappa reaches 0.72 indicating substantial agreement, with the NLI system showing a 6.3% false positive rate and 8.8% false negative rate, while both human and NLI preservation rates hover around 85-87%. For the logistic regression model pooling roughly 450 observations, the formality intercept is significant at p=0.006, the original formality predictor is significant at p=0.046, but the interaction term doesn't reach significance, suggesting the main formality effect is driving the results.\n\nNow I'm thinking through the narrative structure for the overall findings and planning out which experiments contribute to each figure. The main paper will need a problem illustration from the initial experiments, a method overview, the core heatmap results showing judge by benchmark by method comparisons, sensitivity analysis for the NLI threshold, and a decomposition figure breaking down formality effects versus original preference. The appendix will include additional cross-axis comparisons and supporting analyses.\n\nBefore I finalize the YAML, I need to verify the statistical correction for exp-001. With three judges and a Holm correction applied, I'm checking whether at least two-thirds meet the significance threshold of p<0.05 after adjusting for multiple comparisons.\n\nFor exp-002, I'm confirming that the Likert-Pairwise gap replicates across the three benchmarks, checking each one against the criteria that Likert shows no significance while Pairwise does.\n\nFor exp-005, Claude's casual-original subset shows a 63% formal win rate with p=0.07, meeting the requirement for at least one judge to exceed 60% with p<0.10.\n\nFor exp-014, the logistic regression results align with expectations: formality has a significant main effect at p=0.006, while the interaction term is non-significant at p=0.58.\n\nFor exp-006, I'm predicting p<0.001 to satisfy the p<0.01 threshold with the n=500 replication.\n\nFor exp-010, the binarized Likert sign test yields p=0.24, confirming non-significance above the 0.10 cutoff.\n\nAll the core assumptions check out, so now I'm writing the YAML with proper causal reasoning in the result_rationale field to explain why these results emerge in the best tier.\n\nWriting YAML output...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18836,"cache_read_input_tokens":39080,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18836},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c6d18026-a2ac-4168-b144-93c83fdba8b2","uuid":"b7bf293e-7136-4d9d-9177-77723bb1caf8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01FdSDoMyHVmSG5wjYjNgU5m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have the existing dream data and registry metrics. Let me integrate everything and generate the full best-tier predictions, especially for the 5 new D015 experiments (exp-010 through exp-014) and with D015 framing adjustments (tone as negative control).\n\n```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  原始 \"Likert Blindspot\" framing 完全成立。\n  C2 是 primary contribution：exp-010 binarized Likert sign test 不显著 (p=0.24)，确认 gap 是 measurement\n  结构差异而非统计检验选择差异。3 个 judge × 3 个 benchmark 中 7/9 组合出现 Likert-Pairwise gap，\n  无 reverse pattern。C1 作为 application contribution 诚实定位，组件来源全部 acknowledge。\n  C3 降级为 preliminary：formality robust + register 作为第二 working axis + tone/verbosity 作为\n  principled boundary。C4 通过 logistic regression (exp-014) formality 主效应独立显著 (p=0.006)\n  提供 CSD-adjusted win rate 的统计基础。n=500 复制 (exp-006) 消除 sample size 质疑。\n  NLI threshold sensitivity (exp-011) 证明结果在 70%-95% 范围内 robust。\n  Human validation (exp-013) κ=0.72 证明 NLI gate 不是 black box。\n  Headline: \"Standard Likert scoring misses style bias that pairwise comparison\n  detects across 3 judges and 3 benchmarks — a structural measurement limitation,\n  not a statistical artifact, confirmed by binarized Likert control.\"\n  Main result table 中 binarized Likert 列提供 C2 决定性证据。\n  25+ refs 到位，projected review score 4.0-4.5，直冲 Main。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-001: Multi-judge formality pairwise\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      在 Claude-3.5-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复现 formality pairwise 实验。\n      使用已生成的 counterfactual pairs (n=100)，每个 judge 做 dual-direction pairwise，\n      position control。与 GPT-4o baseline (69.1%, p=0.006) 对比。\n    expected_results:\n      # GPT-4o (existing baseline)\n      gpt4o_formal_win_rate: 0.691\n      gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.006\n      gpt4o_n_consistent: 55\n      gpt4o_formal_wins: 38\n      gpt4o_casual_wins: 17\n      # Claude-Sonnet (new)\n      claude_sonnet_formal_win_rate: 0.640\n      claude_sonnet_sign_test_p: 0.028\n      claude_sonnet_n_consistent: 50\n      claude_sonnet_formal_wins: 32\n      claude_sonnet_casual_wins: 18\n      claude_sonnet_consistency_rate: 0.51\n      # Gemini-Flash (new)\n      gemini_flash_formal_win_rate: 0.724\n      gemini_flash_sign_test_p: 0.002\n      gemini_flash_n_consistent: 58\n      gemini_flash_formal_wins: 42\n      gemini_flash_casual_wins: 16\n      gemini_flash_consistency_rate: 0.59\n      # Aggregated\n      n_judges_significant_after_holm: 3\n      holm_corrected_p_values:\n        gemini: 0.006  # 0.002 × 3\n        gpt4o: 0.012   # 0.006 × 2\n        claude: 0.028   # 0.028 × 1\n      cross_judge_mean_winrate: 0.685\n      cross_judge_winrate_range: [0.640, 0.724]\n      cross_judge_pairwise_p_median: 0.006\n    result_rationale: >\n      Formality bias 是 LLM judge 的通用现象而非 GPT-4o 特有。三个 judge 的 RLHF 训练数据\n      普遍偏向 formal/professional 风格回答，formal text 与 higher-quality content 在 pretraining\n      语料中高度相关。Claude-Sonnet 效应略弱 (0.64) 因为 Anthropic 的 RLHF 有更多 helpfulness\n      导向校准，对 surface style 依赖稍低；Gemini-Flash 效应略强 (0.72) 因为轻量模型更依赖\n      surface heuristics 作为 quality proxy。三者量级差异 (0.64-0.72) 本身也是 C3 evidence——\n      bias magnitude 是 judge-dependent 的。Holm correction 后全部 p<0.05，因为每个 judge 的\n      raw p 都足够小 (最大 0.028)，3 重比较惩罚不足以翻转。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 2: Formality Pairwise Results Across Judges (LLMBar, n=100)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"n_consistent\", \"Formal Wins\", \"Casual Wins\", \"Win Rate\", \"95% CI\", \"Sign Test p\", \"Holm p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", 55, 38, 17, \"69.1%\", \"[56.0%, 79.7%]\", \"0.006**\", \"0.012*\"]\n          - [\"Claude-Sonnet\", 50, 32, 18, \"64.0%\", \"[50.1%, 75.9%]\", \"0.028*\", \"0.028*\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-Flash\", 58, 42, 16, \"72.4%\", \"[59.8%, 82.3%]\", \"0.002**\", \"0.006**\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 3 (partial): 3×3 heatmap 的 LLMBar 列。色阶从 50% (neutral) 到 75% (strong bias)，\n        三个 judge 均深色，视觉化 cross-judge 一致性。\n    analysis: >\n      A1 假设成立：3/3 judge 在 Holm correction 后显著。cross_judge_mean_winrate 0.685 在\n      [0.60, 0.75] 范围中上。Judge 间量级差异 (Gemini > GPT-4o > Claude) 稳定，\n      为 C3 axis-dependency 提供 judge 维度证据。Direction asymmetry 在所有 judge 上存在\n      (formal-original 方向更强)，为 exp-005 original preference 控制提供动机。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-002: Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 上运行 CSD 流程。新 counterfactual generation (不同 source text)。\n      三个 judge (GPT-4o, Claude-Sonnet, Gemini-Flash) 分别评测。每个 benchmark n=100。\n      与 LLMBar 结果交叉比较，形成 3×3 矩阵。\n    expected_results:\n      # AlpacaEval\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_formal_winrate: 0.670\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_p: 0.012\n      alpacaeval_claude_formal_winrate: 0.610\n      alpacaeval_claude_p: 0.048\n      alpacaeval_gemini_formal_winrate: 0.700\n      alpacaeval_gemini_p: 0.004\n      alpacaeval_counterfactual_nli_pass: 0.90\n      alpacaeval_nli_mean: 0.908\n      # MT-Bench\n      mtbench_gpt4o_formal_winrate: 0.650\n      mtbench_gpt4o_p: 0.018\n      mtbench_claude_formal_winrate: 0.600\n      mtbench_claude_p: 0.065\n      mtbench_gemini_formal_winrate: 0.680\n      mtbench_gemini_p: 0.008\n      mtbench_counterfactual_nli_pass: 0.87\n      mtbench_nli_mean: 0.882\n      # Cross-benchmark aggregated\n      n_benchmarks_with_gap: 3\n      significant_combos_total: 7\n      total_combos: 9\n      non_significant_combos: [\"Claude×MT-Bench (p=0.065, borderline)\"]\n      borderline_combos: 1\n      mean_winrate_across_all_9: 0.664\n    result_rationale: >\n      Formality bias 跨 benchmark 泛化，因为 bias 源于 judge 内在偏好而非特定数据集特征。\n      AlpacaEval 效应略强于 MT-Bench：open-ended instruction-following 任务给 style variation\n      更大空间，formal tone 作为 quality proxy 权重更大；MT-Bench 的 multi-turn 结构和更 specific\n      的评判标准 (如 math/reasoning accuracy) 部分抑制了 style 影响。Claude×MT-Bench 是唯一\n      borderline 不显著的组合 (p=0.065)，因为 Claude 在有明确正确性标准的 benchmark 上更倾向\n      content-based 判断，且 Claude 本身 formality sensitivity 最低。NLI pass rate 在\n      AlpacaEval (0.90) 略高于 MT-Bench (0.87)，因为 AlpacaEval response 结构更简单，\n      counterfactual 改写更容易保持语义。7/9 显著远超偶然水平。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 3: Formality Pairwise Win Rate Matrix (Judge × Benchmark)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"LLMBar\", \"AlpacaEval\", \"MT-Bench\", \"Mean\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"69.1%**\", \"67.0%*\", \"65.0%*\", \"67.0%\"]\n          - [\"Claude-Sonnet\", \"64.0%*\", \"61.0%*\", \"60.0%†\", \"61.7%\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-Flash\", \"72.4%**\", \"70.0%**\", \"68.0%**\", \"70.1%\"]\n          - [\"Mean\", \"68.5%\", \"66.0%\", \"64.3%\", \"66.3%\"]\n        footnote: \"** p<0.01, * p<0.05, † p<0.10. n=100 per cell, n_consistent varies 48-58.\"\n      - title: \"Table 4: Counterfactual Quality per Benchmark\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"n\", \"NLI Pass Rate\", \"NLI Mean\", \"BERTScore Mean\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LLMBar\", 100, \"88%\", 0.896, 0.842]\n          - [\"AlpacaEval\", 100, \"90%\", 0.908, 0.851]\n          - [\"MT-Bench\", 100, \"87%\", 0.882, 0.835]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 3 (main): 3 judges × 3 benchmarks heatmap，cell 内标注 win rate 和显著性星号。\n        色阶：50%=白色, 60%=浅蓝, 70%=深蓝, 80%=深色。视觉传达 cross-judge × cross-benchmark\n        一致的 formality premium。唯一浅色 cell 是 Claude×MT-Bench (60.0%†)。\n    analysis: >\n      A2 假设成立：3/3 benchmarks 显示 gap。Benchmark 梯度 (LLMBar > AlpacaEval > MT-Bench)\n      有方法论意义——task-specific evaluation criteria 越强，style bias 越被抑制。\n      Judge 梯度 (Gemini > GPT-4o > Claude) 稳定跨 benchmark，说明 judge 的 style sensitivity\n      是其内在属性而非 benchmark artifact。9 个组合的 mean win rate 0.664 在\n      cross_judge_formal_win_rate [0.60, 0.75] 范围内。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-003: Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      对 exp-001/002 的每个 judge×benchmark 组合，计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise win rate，\n      系统性比较两种 measurement 的 sensitivity。同一 counterfactual 数据。\n    expected_results:\n      # LLMBar\n      llmbar_gpt4o_likert_ate: 0.10\n      llmbar_gpt4o_likert_p: 0.332\n      llmbar_gpt4o_pairwise_p: 0.006\n      llmbar_claude_likert_ate: 0.06\n      llmbar_claude_likert_p: 0.485\n      llmbar_claude_pairwise_p: 0.028\n      llmbar_gemini_likert_ate: 0.14\n      llmbar_gemini_likert_p: 0.198\n      llmbar_gemini_pairwise_p: 0.002\n      # AlpacaEval\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_likert_ate: 0.08\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_likert_p: 0.412\n      alpacaeval_claude_likert_ate: 0.04\n      alpacaeval_claude_likert_p: 0.551\n      alpacaeval_gemini_likert_ate: 0.12\n      alpacaeval_gemini_likert_p: 0.142\n      # MT-Bench\n      mtbench_gpt4o_likert_ate: 0.09\n      mtbench_gpt4o_likert_p: 0.388\n      mtbench_claude_likert_ate: 0.03\n      mtbench_claude_likert_p: 0.612\n      mtbench_gemini_likert_ate: 0.11\n      mtbench_gemini_likert_p: 0.175\n      # Aggregated gap metrics\n      combos_with_gap: 7\n      combos_without_gap: 2\n      combos_total: 9\n      gap_note: \"2 个无 gap：Claude×MT-Bench (两者都不显著，一致性 non-sig)，Gemini×AlpacaEval Likert p=0.142 borderline\"\n      median_likert_p: 0.388\n      median_pairwise_p: 0.012\n      cross_judge_likert_ate_p_median: 0.37\n      no_reverse_pattern: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Likert-Pairwise gap 的根因是 measurement scale 的信息结构差异。Likert pointwise 评分中，\n      style bias 被三个机制稀释：(1) score anchoring——judge 倾向使用量表中段，微小 style 偏好\n      不足以跨越 score boundary；(2) absolute calibration noise——不同 item 的 baseline quality\n      差异远大于 style 引入的差异，between-item variance 淹没 within-item style effect；\n      (3) 离散量表的 resolution limit——1-10 scale 上 0.10 的 ATE 被四舍五入吸收。\n      Pairwise 直接呈现 A/B 对比，消除 absolute calibration 问题，将 style 差异放大为\n      forced choice 中的 tie-breaking signal。Gemini 的 Likert p (0.142-0.198) 最接近显著，\n      因为 Gemini 的 formality premium 最强 (72.4%)，即使 Likert 的稀释也无法完全消除。\n      但仍未达 p<0.05，确认 Likert blindspot 的系统性。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 5: Likert ATE vs Pairwise Win Rate — The Likert Blindspot\"\n        columns: [\"Judge × Benchmark\", \"Likert ATE\", \"Likert p\", \"Pairwise WR\", \"Pairwise p\", \"Gap?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o × LLMBar\", \"+0.10\", \"0.332\", \"69.1%\", \"0.006**\", \"✓\"]\n          - [\"Claude × LLMBar\", \"+0.06\", \"0.485\", \"64.0%\", \"0.028*\", \"✓\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × LLMBar\", \"+0.14\", \"0.198\", \"72.4%\", \"0.002**\", \"✓\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o × AlpacaEval\", \"+0.08\", \"0.412\", \"67.0%\", \"0.012*\", \"✓\"]\n          - [\"Claude × AlpacaEval\", \"+0.04\", \"0.551\", \"61.0%\", \"0.048*\", \"✓\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × AlpacaEval\", \"+0.12\", \"0.142\", \"70.0%\", \"0.004**\", \"✓\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o × MT-Bench\", \"+0.09\", \"0.388\", \"65.0%\", \"0.018*\", \"✓\"]\n          - [\"Claude × MT-Bench\", \"+0.03\", \"0.612\", \"60.0%\", \"0.065†\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × MT-Bench\", \"+0.11\", \"0.175\", \"68.0%\", \"0.008**\", \"✓\"]\n        footnote: \"Gap = Likert p>0.10 AND Pairwise p<0.05. 7/9 combos show gap. 0/9 reverse pattern.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 1 (main, problem illustration): 双面板对比图。左: Likert ATE 带 95% CI error bar，\n        所有 9 个组合 CI 均跨零线。右: Pairwise win rate 带 Wilson CI，7/9 CI 不含 50%。\n        视觉冲击力：同一数据、两种 measurement、截然不同的结论。\n    analysis: >\n      C2 的核心 evidence。7/9 组合出现系统性 measurement gap，且无 reverse pattern\n      (没有任何组合 Likert 显著但 Pairwise 不显著)。median Likert p = 0.37 在 [0.15, 0.5] 范围内，\n      median Pairwise p = 0.012 在 [0.001, 0.02] 范围内。gap 不依赖特定 judge 或 benchmark——\n      这意味着现有文献中基于 Likert 的 style bias 研究可能系统性低估问题严重程度。\n      Practical implication: style bias audit 应使用 pairwise comparison 而非 pointwise scoring。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-004: Tone axis — NEGATIVE CONTROL\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Tone axis (assertive/hedging) — negative control\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      D014 Tone pilot 已失败 (NLI 65%, joint gate 45%)。Epistemic commitment change 与\n      NLI verification 结构性不兼容。本实验以 pilot 数据 (n=20) 为基础，正式文档化失败模式，\n      作为 C3 的 axis boundary evidence。不需额外 API 调用。\n    expected_results:\n      n_pilot: 20\n      nli_cf_pass_rate: 0.65\n      nli_cf_mean: 0.704\n      bertscore_cf_mean: 0.920\n      joint_pass_rate: 0.45\n      by_tone_assertive_both_pass: 0.385\n      by_tone_hedging_both_pass: 0.571\n      catastrophic_nli_lt001_count: 6\n      catastrophic_fraction: 0.30\n      failure_mode: \"assertive→hedging 改变 epistemic commitment (confidence markers, modal verbs)，NLI 正确检测为 non-entailment\"\n      structural_incompatibility: true\n      pipeline_stopped_at: \"content_verification\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Tone 改变 (assertive↔hedging) 不是纯 style 变换——它改变了说话者对命题的认知承诺程度。\n      \"X is the best approach\" vs \"X might be a reasonable approach\" 在 NLI 框架下不构成双向蕴含，\n      因为前者的 truth conditions 严格强于后者。30% 的样本出现 catastrophic NLI<0.01，\n      说明这不是 threshold 选择问题而是根本性的语义兼容性问题。Hedging 方向 (assertive→hedging)\n      both_pass 更高 (57.1% vs 38.5%)，因为弱化断言仍蕴含弱化后的命题，但强化断言\n      (hedging→assertive) 引入了原文未承诺的确定性。这个不对称性本身就是 principled boundary\n      的证据：NLI gate 不是 arbitrary obstacle，而是正确识别了语义改变。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table A1: Tone Axis Content Verification Failure (n=20 pilot)\"\n        columns: [\"Direction\", \"n\", \"NLI Mean\", \"Both Pass Rate\", \"Catastrophic NLI<0.01\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Assertive→Hedging\", 13, \"0.656\", \"38.5%\", \"4/13 (30.8%)\"]\n          - [\"Hedging→Assertive\", 7, \"0.793\", \"57.1%\", \"2/7 (28.6%)\"]\n          - [\"Overall\", 20, \"0.704\", \"45.0%\", \"6/20 (30.0%)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Appendix Figure: NLI score distribution histogram for tone vs formality counterfactuals。\n        Formality: 右偏，集中在 0.85-1.0。Tone: 双峰分布，一峰在 0.8-1.0 (成功保留)，\n        一峰在 0.0-0.1 (catastrophic failure)。视觉化结构性不兼容。\n    analysis: >\n      Tone 作为 negative control 为 C3 提供 principled method boundary：CSD 适用于\n      不改变认知承诺的 surface-level style axes (formality ✓)，不适用于改变\n      epistemic commitment 的 axes (tone ✗)。NLI gate 在此处正确拒绝——\n      这不是方法失败，而是正确的质量控制行为。Paper 中定位为 \"method boundary\"\n      而非 \"negative result\"，因为它回答了 \"CSD 适用范围\" 这个审稿人一定会问的问题。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-005: Pairwise RATE control (original preference)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Original text vs 同风格 double-rewrite 的 pairwise 比较，量化 original preference confound。\n      D015: 扩展到所有 judge × LLMBar 组合。同时分析 casual-original subset\n      (main pairwise 中原文为 casual 的子集) 在不同 judge 上的 formal win rate。\n    expected_results:\n      # GPT-4o × LLMBar (primary)\n      gpt4o_n_valid: 95\n      gpt4o_n_consistent: 60\n      gpt4o_original_wins: 32\n      gpt4o_rewrite_wins: 28\n      gpt4o_original_win_rate: 0.533\n      gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.362\n      gpt4o_wilson_ci: [0.408, 0.655]\n      # Claude × LLMBar\n      claude_n_consistent: 55\n      claude_original_wins: 28\n      claude_rewrite_wins: 27\n      claude_original_win_rate: 0.509\n      claude_sign_test_p: 0.92\n      # Gemini × LLMBar\n      gemini_n_consistent: 62\n      gemini_original_wins: 34\n      gemini_rewrite_wins: 28\n      gemini_original_win_rate: 0.548\n      gemini_sign_test_p: 0.28\n      # Cross-judge original preference summary\n      mean_original_win_rate: 0.530\n      any_judge_original_pref_significant: false\n      # Casual-original subset (from MAIN pairwise, not RATE)\n      casual_orig_gpt4o_formal_wr: 0.545\n      casual_orig_gpt4o_p: 0.832\n      casual_orig_gpt4o_n: 22\n      casual_orig_claude_formal_wr: 0.630\n      casual_orig_claude_p: 0.072\n      casual_orig_claude_n: 27\n      casual_orig_gemini_formal_wr: 0.611\n      casual_orig_gemini_p: 0.096\n      casual_orig_gemini_n: 36\n      casual_orig_best_judge: \"Claude\"\n      casual_orig_best_judge_wr: 0.630\n      casual_orig_best_judge_p: 0.072\n    result_rationale: >\n      Original preference 在所有 judge 上均弱且不显著 (mean 53.0%)，因为 double-rewrite 过程\n      虽引入轻微 rewrite artifact (如稍微不自然的措辞)，但这个 artifact 对 judge 影响是随机的\n      而非系统性的。Claude 的 original preference 最弱 (50.9%)，可能因为 Claude 对 \"naturalness\"\n      的敏感度更低。Gemini 稍高 (54.8%)，可能因为轻量模型对 fluency 微妙差异更敏感。\n      Casual-original subset 分析是关键：Claude 上 63.0% formal win rate (p=0.072)\n      说明即使 formality preference 与 original preference 方向相反 (formal = rewrite)，\n      formality 仍占上风。这在 GPT-4o 上不显著 (54.5%) 可能因为 GPT-4o 的 original preference\n      (53.3%) 与 formality preference 恰好在 casual-original subset 上互相抵消。\n      Claude original preference 更弱 (50.9%)，所以 formality 更容易 dominate。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 6: Original Preference Control Across Judges (LLMBar)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"n_consistent\", \"Original Wins\", \"Rewrite Wins\", \"Original WR\", \"p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", 60, 32, 28, \"53.3%\", \"0.362\"]\n          - [\"Claude-Sonnet\", 55, 28, 27, \"50.9%\", \"0.920\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-Flash\", 62, 34, 28, \"54.8%\", \"0.280\"]\n      - title: \"Table 7: Casual-Original Subset — Formal Win Rate When Opposing Original Preference\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"n_consistent\", \"Formal Wins\", \"Formal WR\", \"p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", 22, 12, \"54.5%\", \"0.832\"]\n          - [\"Claude-Sonnet\", 27, 17, \"63.0%\", \"0.072†\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-Flash\", 36, 22, \"61.1%\", \"0.096†\"]\n        footnote: \"† p<0.10. Formal = rewrite in this subset, so original preference opposes formality.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 5 (partial): Effect decomposition bar chart。三组柱状图 (GPT-4o, Claude, Gemini)，\n        每组两柱：total formal WR (tall, ~65-72%) vs original preference WR (short, ~51-55%)。\n        差值区间标注 \"formality-attributable effect\"。\n    analysis: >\n      A6 假设成立：original preference 贡献 <5 个百分点 (mean 53% - 50% = 3%)，\n      远小于 formality premium (mean 68.5% - 50% = 18.5%)。Casual-original subset\n      在 Claude (63%) 和 Gemini (61.1%) 上均 >60%，best judge p=0.072 满足 p<0.10。\n      casual_orig_best_judge_wr 0.63 在 [0.60, 0.70] 范围内。\n      Direction asymmetry (MVP 中 formal-orig 78.8% vs casual-orig 54.5%) 主要解释\n      从 \"original preference\" 转向 \"改写方向的非对称难度\"。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-006: Scaled replication (n=500)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Scaled replication (n=500)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      将 formality pairwise 实验从 n=100 扩大到 n=500。选择效应最强的 judge×benchmark 组合\n      (Gemini×LLMBar)。Power analysis 确定 minimum detectable effect size。\n      五个 n=100 子组的稳定性分析。\n    expected_results:\n      n_total: 500\n      n_valid_both_trials: 490\n      n_consistent: 278\n      consistency_rate: 0.567\n      formal_wins: 184\n      casual_wins: 94\n      formal_win_rate: 0.662\n      wilson_ci: [0.604, 0.716]\n      sign_test_p: 0.00001\n      cohens_h: 0.337\n      # Likert control at n=500\n      likert_ate_n500: 0.11\n      likert_ate_p_n500: 0.082\n      likert_still_borderline: true\n      # Subgroup stability\n      sub1_winrate: 0.70\n      sub2_winrate: 0.65\n      sub3_winrate: 0.68\n      sub4_winrate: 0.64\n      sub5_winrate: 0.64\n      subgroup_sd: 0.026\n      # Power analysis\n      power_n100_d065: 0.72\n      power_n300_d065: 0.97\n      power_n500_d065: 0.995\n      min_detectable_wr_n500: 0.56\n      # NLI stratification\n      nli_ge90_n_consistent: 232\n      nli_ge90_winrate: 0.685\n      nli_ge80_n_consistent: 262\n      nli_ge80_winrate: 0.668\n    result_rationale: >\n      n=500 时 win rate 0.662 相比 n=100 pilot 的 0.691 有 2.9% 的 regression to mean，\n      这在预期范围内——pilot 的 point estimate 在 CI [0.56, 0.80] 上端，larger sample 收敛到\n      true effect。CI 从 [0.56, 0.80] 收窄到 [0.60, 0.72]，p 从 0.006 降到 <0.001。\n      五个 n=100 子组 win rate 在 0.64-0.70 范围波动 (σ=0.026)，展示效应高度稳定。\n      关键发现：即使 n=500，Likert ATE 仍仅 borderline 显著 (p=0.082)——这强化了 C2：\n      Likert blindspot 不是 power 问题，而是 measurement sensitivity 的结构性差异。\n      如果仅仅是 power 问题，n=500 的 Likert 应当显著；它仍不显著说明 Likert 对 style bias\n      的检测本身就是 structurally impaired。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 8: Scaled Replication (Gemini × LLMBar, Formality)\"\n        columns: [\"Scale\", \"n_consistent\", \"Formal WR\", \"95% CI\", \"Pairwise p\", \"Likert p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"n=100 (MVP pilot)\", 55, \"69.1%\", \"[56.0%, 79.7%]\", \"0.006**\", \"0.332\"]\n          - [\"n=500 (replication)\", 278, \"66.2%\", \"[60.4%, 71.6%]\", \"<0.001***\", \"0.082†\"]\n        footnote: \"Likert p still non-significant at n=500 (borderline), confirming structural measurement gap.\"\n      - title: \"Table 9: Subgroup Stability (5 × n=100 splits)\"\n        columns: [\"Split\", \"n_consistent\", \"Formal WR\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Block 1\", 57, \"70.0%\"]\n          - [\"Block 2\", 53, \"65.0%\"]\n          - [\"Block 3\", 56, \"68.0%\"]\n          - [\"Block 4\", 54, \"64.0%\"]\n          - [\"Block 5\", 58, \"64.0%\"]\n          - [\"Full n=500\", 278, \"66.2%\"]\n      - title: \"Table 10: Power Analysis\"\n        columns: [\"n\", \"Power (WR=0.65)\", \"Min Detectable WR (power=0.80)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [100, \"0.72\", \"62.0%\"]\n          - [300, \"0.97\", \"57.5%\"]\n          - [500, \"0.995\", \"56.0%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Appendix Figure: Forest plot 展示 5 个 n=100 blocks 的 formal win rate + 95% Wilson CI，\n        底部 diamond 标注 pooled estimate。所有 CI 互相重叠且不含 50%，视觉化效应稳定性。\n    analysis: >\n      n500_formal_win_rate 0.662 在 [0.58, 0.70] 范围内。p<0.001 满足 p<0.01 核心假设。\n      n=500 Likert 仍 borderline (p=0.082) 是 C2 的额外弹药——即使 5× sample size 都不能\n      让 Likert 检测到 pairwise 在 n=100 就发现的效应。Power analysis 解释了 why：\n      pairwise within-subject design 的 effective sample size 远大于 Likert between-subject。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-008: Register axis (academic/conversational)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Register axis (academic/conversational)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      第三个 surface-level axis 测试。Academic vs conversational register 改变词汇和句法\n      但不改变信息内容。Full pipeline: counterfactual gen → NLI verification → dual-direction\n      pairwise scoring。三个 judge × LLMBar，n=100。\n    expected_results:\n      register_nli_pass_rate: 0.86\n      register_nli_mean: 0.893\n      register_bertscore_mean: 0.839\n      register_both_pass: 0.83\n      # Per-judge\n      gpt4o_academic_win_rate: 0.660\n      gpt4o_n_consistent: 53\n      gpt4o_p: 0.015\n      claude_academic_win_rate: 0.620\n      claude_n_consistent: 50\n      claude_p: 0.042\n      gemini_academic_win_rate: 0.714\n      gemini_n_consistent: 56\n      gemini_p: 0.003\n      judges_significant: 3\n      mean_academic_winrate: 0.665\n      # Likert control\n      gpt4o_likert_p: 0.289\n      claude_likert_p: 0.511\n      gemini_likert_p: 0.167\n      register_likert_pairwise_gap: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Register (academic vs conversational) 是 surface-level 词汇+句法变换，不改变信息内容：\n      Latinate 术语 vs everyday words, 复杂从句 vs 简单句, disciplinary jargon vs lay terms。\n      效应在 formality 和 tone 之间 (mean 0.665)，因为 register 涉及词汇和句法层面变化\n      但比 formality 更窄——formality 包含 register + tone + 其他 cues 的 composite。\n      NLI pass 0.86 略低于 formality (0.88)，因为 academic vocabulary 有时引入微妙语义偏移\n      (术语替代 layman terms 可能 shift specificity)。Judge 梯度保持 Gemini > GPT-4o > Claude，\n      进一步确认这是 judge 内在属性而非 axis-specific 现象。所有 Likert p 均不显著，\n      扩展了 C2 blindspot evidence 到第二个 axis。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table A2: Register (Academic vs Conversational) Pairwise Results (LLMBar)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"n_consistent\", \"Academic Wins\", \"Conv. Wins\", \"Win Rate\", \"Pairwise p\", \"Likert p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", 53, 35, 18, \"66.0%\", \"0.015*\", \"0.289\"]\n          - [\"Claude-Sonnet\", 50, 31, 19, \"62.0%\", \"0.042*\", \"0.511\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-Flash\", 56, 40, 16, \"71.4%\", \"0.003**\", \"0.167\"]\n      - title: \"Table A3: Cross-Axis Summary (LLMBar, 3 judges)\"\n        columns: [\"Axis\", \"Mean WR\", \"Judges Sig. (3)\", \"NLI Pass\", \"Likert Detects?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Formality\", \"68.5%\", \"3/3\", \"88%\", \"0/3\"]\n          - [\"Register\", \"66.5%\", \"3/3\", \"86%\", \"0/3\"]\n          - [\"Tone\", \"—\", \"—\", \"65% (failed)\", \"N/A\"]\n          - [\"Verbosity\", \"—\", \"—\", \"65% (failed)\", \"N/A\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Appendix Figure: Cross-axis bar chart。四个 axes，每个三柱 (GPT-4o, Claude, Gemini)。\n        Formality 和 Register 均高于 50% baseline，Tone 和 Verbosity 标注 \"Failed H1\"。\n        视觉化 CSD 的 axis-dependent 有效性。\n    analysis: >\n      Register 作为第二个 working axis 将 C3 从 \"only formality works\" 提升为\n      \"content-preserving surface-level axes generally work\"。效应量级系统性排序\n      formality > register > (tone/verbosity failed)，与 linguistic level 数量正相关：\n      formality 跨词汇+句法+语用，register 跨词汇+句法，tone 主要在语用层。\n      这提供了 principled taxonomy：改变 surface form 而不改变 information content\n      或 epistemic commitment 的 axes 适用于 CSD。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-009: Non-Qwen rewriter control\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      使用 Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct 作为替代 rewriter，对 LLMBar formality 运行完整 pipeline。\n      与 Qwen3-32B 结果比较，排除 Qwen-family artifacts。GPT-4o 作为 judge。\n    expected_results:\n      llama_nli_pass_rate: 0.85\n      llama_nli_mean: 0.881\n      llama_bertscore_mean: 0.836\n      llama_n_consistent: 52\n      llama_formal_win_rate: 0.660\n      llama_sign_test_p: 0.015\n      # Comparison with Qwen\n      qwen_nli_pass_rate: 0.88\n      qwen_formal_win_rate: 0.691\n      qwen_sign_test_p: 0.006\n      winrate_difference: 0.031\n      fisher_exact_p_for_difference: 0.42\n      rewriter_effect_significant: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      Llama rewriter 产生略低但仍显著的 formality premium (0.66 vs 0.69)，差异不显著\n      (Fisher p=0.42)。NLI pass rate 略低 (0.85 vs 0.88) 因为 Llama-70B 在 instruction\n      following 上略弱于 Qwen3-32B (后者受益于 Qwen3 的强 instruction tuning)，导致少量\n      counterfactual 有轻微语义偏移。3% win rate 差异在统计噪声范围内，排除了\n      \"Qwen rewriter 引入某种被 judge 偏好的 writing pattern\" 的 confound。\n      关键论点：formality bias 检测不依赖于特定 rewriter family。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table A4: Rewriter Ablation (GPT-4o × LLMBar, Formality)\"\n        columns: [\"Rewriter\", \"NLI Pass\", \"Formal WR\", \"Pairwise p\", \"n_consistent\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B\", \"88%\", \"69.1%\", \"0.006**\", 55]\n          - [\"Llama-3.1-70B\", \"85%\", \"66.0%\", \"0.015*\", 52]\n          - [\"Difference\", \"-3%\", \"-3.1%\", \"Fisher p=0.42\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Appendix 级实验，但对 reviewer 质疑 rewriter choice 时提供决定性回应。\n      两个不同 family 的 rewriter 产生一致的 formality premium，确认效应的 robustness。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-010: Binarized Likert sign test (C2 CRITICAL CONTROL)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Binarized Likert sign test (C2 critical control)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: >\n      DREAM CRITICAL。对已有 scored_32b.jsonl 数据做 sign test：每对中 formal version 的\n      Likert score 是否严格高于 casual version？如果 binarized Likert sign test 也显著 →\n      gap 是 test choice 差异，非 measurement method 差异。如果不显著 → 确认 C2。\n      零成本重分析。\n    expected_results:\n      data_source: \"scored_32b.jsonl (GPT-4o × LLMBar, n=88 primary)\"\n      n_primary: 88\n      n_formal_higher: 29\n      n_casual_higher: 21\n      n_tied: 38\n      tie_fraction: 0.432\n      n_non_tied: 50\n      binarized_formal_rate: 0.580\n      sign_test_p: 0.24\n      is_significant: false\n      # Sensitivity: different score difference thresholds\n      strict_binarize_diff_ge2:\n        n_non_tied: 18\n        formal_wins: 11\n        sign_test_p: 0.48\n      # For comparison\n      pairwise_formal_wr: 0.691\n      pairwise_p: 0.006\n      gap_confirmed: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Binarized Likert 不显著 (p=0.24) 的根因是 Likert scale 的 discretization loss。\n      在 1-10 量表上，formality 引入的 quality perception 差异约 0.10 分 (从 Likert ATE)，\n      这远小于一个 scale step。因此 43.2% 的 pair 获得相同 Likert score (tied)——这些\n      pair 中 judge 确实感知到了 formality 差异 (pairwise 中会做出选择)，但 Likert 的\n      粗粒度量表无法捕捉这个差异。在 50 个 non-tied pairs 中，formal 略占优 (58%) 但\n      sample size 太小 (n=50 而非 pairwise 的 n=55 consistent)，sign test power 不足。\n      即使用更严格的 binarization (score difference ≥ 2)，n 降到 18，formal 11/18 (61%)\n      但 p=0.48 更加不显著。关键 insight: pairwise 的 forced-choice 消除了 tie 问题——\n      judge 必须在两个版本间选择，将 Likert 中被 tie 掩盖的微弱偏好显现出来。\n      这证明 Likert-Pairwise gap 是 measurement granularity 差异，非 statistical test 选择差异。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 11: Binarized Likert vs Pairwise — C2 Decisive Test\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"n (non-tied/consistent)\", \"Formal Rate\", \"Sign Test p\", \"Conclusion\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Pairwise (position-controlled)\", 55, \"69.1%\", \"0.006**\", \"Significant bias detected\"]\n          - [\"Binarized Likert (score > comparison)\", 50, \"58.0%\", \"0.240\", \"Not significant\"]\n          - [\"Binarized Likert (diff ≥ 2)\", 18, \"61.1%\", \"0.481\", \"Not significant\"]\n        footnote: \"Same underlying data (scored_32b.jsonl). Pairwise detects what binarized Likert misses.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 4 (or Figure 1 panel C): 三柱对比图。柱1: Pairwise formal rate 69.1% (显著, 深色)。\n        柱2: Binarized Likert formal rate 58.0% (不显著, 浅色)。柱3: Raw Likert ATE p=0.33\n        (不显著, 浅色)。标注 \"43% of Likert pairs tied — pairwise breaks ties\"。\n        这是 C2 的 visual proof。\n    analysis: >\n      THIS IS THE DECISIVE EVIDENCE FOR C2。binarized_likert_sign_p = 0.24 在 [0.12, 1.0] 范围内。\n      排除了 \"Likert 和 Pairwise 用不同 statistical test 所以不可比\" 的 alternative explanation。\n      现在三种分析都使用 sign test on binary outcome，唯一差异是 measurement method：\n      (1) Pairwise forced-choice → 69.1%, p=0.006\n      (2) Binarized Likert score comparison → 58.0%, p=0.24\n      (3) Raw Likert ATE → p=0.33\n      Pairwise 胜出是因为它消除了 Likert 的 tie problem (43% tied) 和 between-item calibration noise。\n      Main Result Table 中增加 Binarized Likert 列是 C2 的命门证据。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-011: NLI threshold sensitivity analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"NLI threshold sensitivity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-011\"\n    description: >\n      在 70%, 75%, 80%, 85%, 90%, 95% 六个 NLI threshold 上重新计算 formality pairwise results。\n      验证结论对 threshold 选择的 robustness。零成本重分析已有 pairwise_32b 数据。\n    expected_results:\n      data_source: \"pairwise_results_32b.jsonl (GPT-4o × LLMBar)\"\n      thresholds:\n        nli_70:\n          n_pairs_pass: 96\n          n_consistent: 53\n          formal_wins: 37\n          formal_wr: 0.698\n          sign_test_p: 0.005\n        nli_75:\n          n_pairs_pass: 94\n          n_consistent: 52\n          formal_wins: 36\n          formal_wr: 0.692\n          sign_test_p: 0.006\n        nli_80:\n          n_pairs_pass: 88\n          n_consistent: 50\n          formal_wins: 35\n          formal_wr: 0.700\n          sign_test_p: 0.005\n        nli_85:\n          n_pairs_pass: 72\n          n_consistent: 42\n          formal_wins: 31\n          formal_wr: 0.738\n          sign_test_p: 0.003\n        nli_90:\n          n_pairs_pass: 52\n          n_consistent: 46\n          formal_wins: 34\n          formal_wr: 0.739\n          sign_test_p: 0.002\n        nli_95:\n          n_pairs_pass: 36\n          n_consistent: 28\n          formal_wins: 21\n          formal_wr: 0.750\n          sign_test_p: 0.013\n      all_significant_70_to_95: true\n      winrate_trend: \"monotonically increasing (0.698 → 0.750)\"\n      p_value_trend: \"decreasing then increasing (0.005 → 0.002 → 0.013) due to n tradeoff\"\n      significant_range: \"70%-95%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Formality effect 在所有 NLI threshold 上均显著，因为 formality 改写是高质量的 surface-level\n      变换——即使在宽松 threshold (70%) 下加入的额外 pairs 中有一些 semantic drift，\n      formality premium 仍然 dominant。Win rate 随 threshold 提高而单调递增 (0.698→0.750)，\n      说明 cleaner pairs (higher NLI) 的 formality effect 更纯——content preservation 越好，\n      observed bias 越接近 true causal effect。p 值在 85-90% 处最低 (0.002)，因为此处\n      n (42-46) 与 effect size (0.74) 达到最佳平衡；95% threshold 下 n 降到 28，\n      尽管 effect size 最高 (0.75)，power 损失导致 p 略升至 0.013，但仍远低于 0.05。\n      Tone 的 NLI 在 72% 处 borderline——sensitivity analysis 显示即使在 70% threshold 下\n      formality 仍稳健，这不是 threshold tuning 的结果。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 12: NLI Threshold Sensitivity (GPT-4o × LLMBar, Formality Pairwise)\"\n        columns: [\"NLI Threshold\", \"n_pass\", \"n_consistent\", \"Formal WR\", \"Sign Test p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"≥70%\", 96, 53, \"69.8%\", \"0.005**\"]\n          - [\"≥75%\", 94, 52, \"69.2%\", \"0.006**\"]\n          - [\"≥80%\", 88, 50, \"70.0%\", \"0.005**\"]\n          - [\"≥85%\", 72, 42, \"73.8%\", \"0.003**\"]\n          - [\"≥90%\", 52, 46, \"73.9%\", \"0.002**\"]\n          - [\"≥95%\", 36, 28, \"75.0%\", \"0.013*\"]\n        footnote: \"All thresholds from 70% to 95% yield significant results. Default threshold: 80%.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 4: 双 Y 轴折线图。X 轴: NLI threshold (70%-95%)。左 Y 轴 (蓝线): formal win rate，\n        缓慢上升。右 Y 轴 (红线): -log10(p)，先升后降 (n-effect size tradeoff)。\n        水平虚线标注 p=0.05。所有 threshold 点均在虚线之上。阴影区标注 \"default threshold\"。\n    analysis: >\n      nli_threshold_sensitivity_significant_range = ['70%-95%']，完美匹配核心假设。\n      结论不依赖 threshold 选择——从最宽松 (70%) 到最严格 (95%) 均显著。\n      Win rate 随 threshold 上升这一 monotonic trend 说明 content preservation quality\n      与 formality effect purity 正相关，支持 CSD 的 causal interpretation。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-012: Consistency filter bias analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Consistency filter bias analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-012\"\n    description: >\n      比较 position-consistent pairs vs inconsistent pairs 的 NLI scores、text lengths、\n      task types，检查 42-52% 的 discard rate 是否引入系统性偏差。零成本重分析。\n    expected_results:\n      data_source: \"pairwise_results_32b.jsonl\"\n      total_valid_pairs: 98\n      n_consistent: 55\n      n_inconsistent: 43\n      discard_rate: 0.439\n      # NLI comparison\n      consistent_nli_mean: 0.903\n      inconsistent_nli_mean: 0.886\n      nli_ttest_p: 0.42\n      nli_difference_significant: false\n      # Text length comparison\n      consistent_text_length_mean: 142.3\n      inconsistent_text_length_mean: 137.8\n      length_ttest_p: 0.58\n      length_difference_significant: false\n      # Original style distribution\n      consistent_formal_orig_fraction: 0.600\n      inconsistent_formal_orig_fraction: 0.558\n      orig_style_chi2_p: 0.67\n      orig_style_difference_significant: false\n      # BERTScore comparison\n      consistent_bertscore_mean: 0.848\n      inconsistent_bertscore_mean: 0.834\n      bertscore_ttest_p: 0.38\n      bertscore_difference_significant: false\n      # Task type distribution (chi-square)\n      task_type_chi2_p: 0.73\n      task_type_difference_significant: false\n      # Conclusion\n      any_significant_difference: false\n      filter_introduces_bias: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      Position-consistency filtering 不引入系统性偏差，因为 position inconsistency 的主要来源\n      是 judge 的 confidence 而非 pair 的 systematic properties。Judge 对某些 pairs 有明确偏好\n      (无论位置如何都选同一个) → consistent，对另一些 pairs 犹豫不决 (位置影响选择) → inconsistent。\n      犹豫不决与 pair 的 NLI、text length、task type 无关，而与 quality 差异的微妙程度有关——\n      当两个版本在 judge 眼中 \"差不多好\" 时，position 成为 tie-breaker。这是随机噪声，\n      不是对特定类型 pair 的系统性过滤。NLI 略高 (0.903 vs 0.886) 但 p=0.42 不显著，\n      说明 content preservation 质量不驱动 consistency。consistent pairs 中 formal-original\n      fraction (0.60) 略高于 inconsistent (0.56)，但差异远不显著 (p=0.67)，排除了\n      \"filtering selects for original-preference-aligned pairs\" 的 confound。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table A5: Consistency Filter Bias Analysis (GPT-4o × LLMBar)\"\n        columns: [\"Property\", \"Consistent (n=55)\", \"Inconsistent (n=43)\", \"Test\", \"p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"NLI Mean\", \"0.903\", \"0.886\", \"t-test\", \"0.42\"]\n          - [\"Text Length (words)\", \"142.3\", \"137.8\", \"t-test\", \"0.58\"]\n          - [\"BERTScore Mean\", \"0.848\", \"0.834\", \"t-test\", \"0.38\"]\n          - [\"Formal-Original %\", \"60.0%\", \"55.8%\", \"χ²\", \"0.67\"]\n          - [\"Task Type Distribution\", \"—\", \"—\", \"χ²\", \"0.73\"]\n        footnote: \"No significant differences. Consistency filtering does not systematically bias the retained sample.\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      所有 5 个 comparison 均不显著 (最小 p=0.38)，conclusively 排除 systematic filter bias。\n      42-52% 的 discard rate 虽高，但 discarded pairs 与 retained pairs 在 observables 上\n      indistinguishable。Reviewer 对 \"high discard rate → biased sample\" 的 concern\n      可用此表直接回应。建议放在 Appendix 作为 methodological robustness check。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-013: Human NLI validation\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Human NLI validation (80 annotations)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-013\"\n    description: >\n      Human validation of NLI gate decisions。对 80 个 counterfactual pairs 做人工标注：\n      content 是否 preserved。报告 human-NLI agreement (Cohen's κ)。\n      可使用 LLM-as-annotator (GPT-4) + human spot check 的混合策略。\n    expected_results:\n      n_annotated: 80\n      # Sampling strategy\n      n_nli_high: 50  # NLI ≥ 0.85 (expected to pass)\n      n_nli_low: 30   # NLI < 0.85 (expected to fail)\n      # Human judgments\n      human_preserved: 62\n      human_not_preserved: 18\n      human_preservation_rate: 0.775\n      # NLI judgments (at threshold 0.80)\n      nli_preserved: 58\n      nli_not_preserved: 22\n      # Agreement matrix\n      both_preserved: 54\n      both_not_preserved: 14\n      nli_preserved_human_not: 4\n      nli_not_preserved_human_yes: 8\n      # Agreement metrics\n      raw_agreement: 0.850\n      cohens_kappa: 0.72\n      kappa_interpretation: \"substantial agreement\"\n      # Error analysis\n      nli_false_positive_rate: 0.069  # 4/58 NLI says preserved but human disagrees\n      nli_false_negative_rate: 0.129  # 8/62 NLI says not preserved but human says preserved\n      # Qualitative error patterns\n      false_positive_pattern: \"subtle information additions in formal rewrites that NLI misses\"\n      false_negative_pattern: \"stylistic paraphrases that NLI over-penalizes as semantic change\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cohen's κ = 0.72 (substantial agreement) 因为 NLI 模型 (DeBERTa-large-MNLI) 的 training data\n      与 content preservation 判断高度对齐——NLI 本质上就是判断两个文本是否表达相同信息，\n      这与 \"counterfactual 是否保持 content\" 的判断完全一致。False positive rate 低 (6.9%)\n      说明 NLI gate 通过的 pairs 绝大多数确实 content-preserved——这是 CSD 结论可信度的基础。\n      False negative rate 较高 (12.9%) 说明 NLI 偏保守 (over-reject)，但这对 CSD 是安全的方向：\n      over-rejection 意味着 retained pairs 的 content preservation 质量比 NLI score 建议的更高。\n      8 个 false negative 主要是 stylistic paraphrasing (如换用近义词或调整句子结构) 被 NLI\n      判为 non-entailment，但人工判断这些改变不影响信息内容。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table A6: Human-NLI Agreement on Content Preservation (n=80)\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"Human: Preserved\", \"Human: Not Preserved\", \"Total\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"NLI: Preserved (≥0.80)\", 54, 4, 58]\n          - [\"NLI: Not Preserved (<0.80)\", 8, 14, 22]\n          - [\"Total\", 62, 18, 80]\n        footnote: \"Cohen's κ = 0.72 (substantial agreement). NLI FPR = 6.9%, FNR = 12.9%.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Appendix Figure: Scatter plot，X 轴 NLI score (0-1)，Y 轴 human preservation judgment\n        (binary, jittered)。标注 threshold 垂直线在 0.80。右上象限 (both agree: preserved)\n        最密集，左下象限 (both agree: not preserved) 次之。右下 (NLI high, human not) = 4 点\n        标注为 false positives。展示 NLI score 与 human judgment 的一致性。\n    analysis: >\n      κ = 0.72 在 [0.61, 0.80] \"substantial\" 范围内，满足审稿人对 NLI gate 可信度的要求。\n      NLI 偏保守 (FNR > FPR) 对 CSD 有利：retained pairs 的 content preservation 质量\n      被 underestimate 而非 overestimate。建议论文中强调：\"NLI false positives are rare (6.9%),\n      meaning pairs that pass the gate genuinely preserve content.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-014: Logistic regression for original-preference decomposition\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Formal statistical model for original-preference decomposition\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-014\"\n    description: >\n      Logistic regression 正式分离 formality 和 original preference。\n      Pool exp-001/002 所有 judge×benchmark pairwise 数据。DV: formal_preferred (1/0)。\n      IV: is_formal_original (1/0), judge (fixed effects), benchmark (fixed effects)。\n      Test formality 主效应 (intercept) 是否显著，interaction 是否不显著。\n    expected_results:\n      data_source: \"pooled pairwise from all judge × benchmark combinations\"\n      n_observations: 459  # ~51 consistent per combo × 9 combos\n      # Model: logit(P(formal_preferred)) = β₀ + β₁·is_formal_original + judge_FE + benchmark_FE\n      intercept_beta: 0.52\n      intercept_se: 0.19\n      intercept_z: 2.74\n      intercept_p: 0.006\n      intercept_odds_ratio: 1.68\n      intercept_interpretation: \"formal 被偏好的 odds 是 casual 的 1.68 倍，controlling for original status\"\n      # is_formal_original coefficient\n      is_formal_original_beta: 0.34\n      is_formal_original_se: 0.17\n      is_formal_original_z: 2.00\n      is_formal_original_p: 0.046\n      is_formal_original_or: 1.40\n      # Interaction term\n      interaction_beta: 0.12\n      interaction_se: 0.22\n      interaction_z: 0.55\n      interaction_p: 0.58\n      interaction_significant: false\n      # Judge fixed effects (relative to GPT-4o)\n      judge_claude_beta: -0.28\n      judge_claude_p: 0.11\n      judge_gemini_beta: 0.19\n      judge_gemini_p: 0.24\n      # Benchmark fixed effects (relative to LLMBar)\n      benchmark_alpacaeval_beta: -0.08\n      benchmark_alpacaeval_p: 0.62\n      benchmark_mtbench_beta: -0.15\n      benchmark_mtbench_p: 0.38\n      # Model fit\n      mcfadden_r2: 0.042\n      aic: 582.3\n      bic: 611.7\n      # CSD-adjusted win rate\n      raw_mean_formal_wr: 0.664\n      original_preference_contribution: 0.033  # from β₁ coefficient\n      csd_adjusted_formal_wr: 0.631  # raw - original_preference_contribution\n      logistic_formality_coef_p: 0.006\n    result_rationale: >\n      Formality 主效应 (intercept β₀=0.52, p=0.006) 显著，说明控制 original status 后\n      formal 仍被系统性偏好——这是 formality bias 作为 independent causal effect 的统计证据。\n      is_formal_original (β₁=0.34, p=0.046) 边缘显著，说明 original preference 确实存在\n      但效应量 (OR=1.40) 远小于 formality (OR=1.68)。关键：interaction term 不显著 (p=0.58)，\n      意味着 formality 的效应不依赖于 formal 版本是否为 original——无论 formal 是原文还是改写，\n      judge 都偏好它。这彻底回应了 \"observed formality bias 只是 original preference 的 proxy\"\n      的 alternative explanation。Judge 和 benchmark fixed effects 不显著，说明\n      formality premium 在不同 judge 和 benchmark 间是 stable 的 (尽管 magnitude 有差异，\n      但 direction 一致)。CSD-adjusted formal win rate = 63.1% (扣除 original preference\n      贡献 3.3 个百分点)，这是对 reviewer 最保守友好的 headline number。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 13: Logistic Regression — Formality vs Original Preference Decomposition\"\n        columns: [\"Predictor\", \"β\", \"SE\", \"z\", \"p\", \"Odds Ratio\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Intercept (formality effect)\", \"0.52\", \"0.19\", \"2.74\", \"0.006**\", \"1.68\"]\n          - [\"is_formal_original\", \"0.34\", \"0.17\", \"2.00\", \"0.046*\", \"1.40\"]\n          - [\"Interaction\", \"0.12\", \"0.22\", \"0.55\", \"0.583\", \"1.13\"]\n          - [\"Judge: Claude (vs GPT-4o)\", \"-0.28\", \"0.17\", \"-1.65\", \"0.110\", \"0.76\"]\n          - [\"Judge: Gemini (vs GPT-4o)\", \"0.19\", \"0.16\", \"1.19\", \"0.240\", \"1.21\"]\n          - [\"Bench: AlpacaEval (vs LLMBar)\", \"-0.08\", \"0.16\", \"-0.50\", \"0.620\", \"0.92\"]\n          - [\"Bench: MT-Bench (vs LLMBar)\", \"-0.15\", \"0.17\", \"-0.88\", \"0.380\", \"0.86\"]\n        footnote: \"N=459 observations pooled across 9 judge×benchmark combinations. McFadden R²=0.042.\"\n      - title: \"Table 14: CSD-Adjusted Win Rate\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\", \"Source\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Raw formal win rate (mean across combos)\", \"66.4%\", \"exp-001/002\"]\n          - [\"Original preference contribution\", \"+3.3%\", \"exp-014 β₁\"]\n          - [\"CSD-adjusted formal win rate\", \"63.1%\", \"Raw − original contribution\"]\n          - [\"95% CI of adjusted rate\", \"[57.2%, 69.0%]\", \"Bootstrap\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 5 (main): Effect decomposition waterfall chart。\n        Bar 1: Raw formal WR = 66.4%。\n        Bar 2: −3.3% (original preference, green downward)。\n        Bar 3: Net formality causal effect = 63.1% (blue, 13.1% above 50% baseline)。\n        Error bars on final bar from bootstrap CI。\n        Visual proof that formality effect survives original preference correction。\n    analysis: >\n      logistic_formality_coef_p = 0.006 在 [0.001, 0.05] 范围内。Interaction p = 0.58\n      明确不显著。C4 (practical guidance) 有了统计基础：CSD-adjusted win rate 公式为\n      adjusted_wr = raw_wr - β₁/(β₀+β₁) × (raw_wr - 0.50)。这比 ad-hoc additive correction\n      更有统计根据。Paper 可以给出 practitioner checklist：(1) use pairwise over Likert for\n      style bias audit; (2) run RATE control to quantify original preference; (3) report both\n      raw and CSD-adjusted win rates; (4) verify content preservation per axis before applying CSD。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18836,"cache_read_input_tokens":39080,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18836},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c6d18026-a2ac-4168-b144-93c83fdba8b2","uuid":"958bde3f-7c88-4a74-a55f-e80a22a11934"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":909006,"duration_api_ms":908195,"num_turns":7,"result":"Now I have the existing dream data and registry metrics. Let me integrate everything and generate the full best-tier predictions, especially for the 5 new D015 experiments (exp-010 through exp-014) and with D015 framing adjustments (tone as negative control).\n\n```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  原始 \"Likert Blindspot\" framing 完全成立。\n  C2 是 primary contribution：exp-010 binarized Likert sign test 不显著 (p=0.24)，确认 gap 是 measurement\n  结构差异而非统计检验选择差异。3 个 judge × 3 个 benchmark 中 7/9 组合出现 Likert-Pairwise gap，\n  无 reverse pattern。C1 作为 application contribution 诚实定位，组件来源全部 acknowledge。\n  C3 降级为 preliminary：formality robust + register 作为第二 working axis + tone/verbosity 作为\n  principled boundary。C4 通过 logistic regression (exp-014) formality 主效应独立显著 (p=0.006)\n  提供 CSD-adjusted win rate 的统计基础。n=500 复制 (exp-006) 消除 sample size 质疑。\n  NLI threshold sensitivity (exp-011) 证明结果在 70%-95% 范围内 robust。\n  Human validation (exp-013) κ=0.72 证明 NLI gate 不是 black box。\n  Headline: \"Standard Likert scoring misses style bias that pairwise comparison\n  detects across 3 judges and 3 benchmarks — a structural measurement limitation,\n  not a statistical artifact, confirmed by binarized Likert control.\"\n  Main result table 中 binarized Likert 列提供 C2 决定性证据。\n  25+ refs 到位，projected review score 4.0-4.5，直冲 Main。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-001: Multi-judge formality pairwise\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      在 Claude-3.5-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复现 formality pairwise 实验。\n      使用已生成的 counterfactual pairs (n=100)，每个 judge 做 dual-direction pairwise，\n      position control。与 GPT-4o baseline (69.1%, p=0.006) 对比。\n    expected_results:\n      # GPT-4o (existing baseline)\n      gpt4o_formal_win_rate: 0.691\n      gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.006\n      gpt4o_n_consistent: 55\n      gpt4o_formal_wins: 38\n      gpt4o_casual_wins: 17\n      # Claude-Sonnet (new)\n      claude_sonnet_formal_win_rate: 0.640\n      claude_sonnet_sign_test_p: 0.028\n      claude_sonnet_n_consistent: 50\n      claude_sonnet_formal_wins: 32\n      claude_sonnet_casual_wins: 18\n      claude_sonnet_consistency_rate: 0.51\n      # Gemini-Flash (new)\n      gemini_flash_formal_win_rate: 0.724\n      gemini_flash_sign_test_p: 0.002\n      gemini_flash_n_consistent: 58\n      gemini_flash_formal_wins: 42\n      gemini_flash_casual_wins: 16\n      gemini_flash_consistency_rate: 0.59\n      # Aggregated\n      n_judges_significant_after_holm: 3\n      holm_corrected_p_values:\n        gemini: 0.006  # 0.002 × 3\n        gpt4o: 0.012   # 0.006 × 2\n        claude: 0.028   # 0.028 × 1\n      cross_judge_mean_winrate: 0.685\n      cross_judge_winrate_range: [0.640, 0.724]\n      cross_judge_pairwise_p_median: 0.006\n    result_rationale: >\n      Formality bias 是 LLM judge 的通用现象而非 GPT-4o 特有。三个 judge 的 RLHF 训练数据\n      普遍偏向 formal/professional 风格回答，formal text 与 higher-quality content 在 pretraining\n      语料中高度相关。Claude-Sonnet 效应略弱 (0.64) 因为 Anthropic 的 RLHF 有更多 helpfulness\n      导向校准，对 surface style 依赖稍低；Gemini-Flash 效应略强 (0.72) 因为轻量模型更依赖\n      surface heuristics 作为 quality proxy。三者量级差异 (0.64-0.72) 本身也是 C3 evidence——\n      bias magnitude 是 judge-dependent 的。Holm correction 后全部 p<0.05，因为每个 judge 的\n      raw p 都足够小 (最大 0.028)，3 重比较惩罚不足以翻转。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 2: Formality Pairwise Results Across Judges (LLMBar, n=100)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"n_consistent\", \"Formal Wins\", \"Casual Wins\", \"Win Rate\", \"95% CI\", \"Sign Test p\", \"Holm p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", 55, 38, 17, \"69.1%\", \"[56.0%, 79.7%]\", \"0.006**\", \"0.012*\"]\n          - [\"Claude-Sonnet\", 50, 32, 18, \"64.0%\", \"[50.1%, 75.9%]\", \"0.028*\", \"0.028*\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-Flash\", 58, 42, 16, \"72.4%\", \"[59.8%, 82.3%]\", \"0.002**\", \"0.006**\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 3 (partial): 3×3 heatmap 的 LLMBar 列。色阶从 50% (neutral) 到 75% (strong bias)，\n        三个 judge 均深色，视觉化 cross-judge 一致性。\n    analysis: >\n      A1 假设成立：3/3 judge 在 Holm correction 后显著。cross_judge_mean_winrate 0.685 在\n      [0.60, 0.75] 范围中上。Judge 间量级差异 (Gemini > GPT-4o > Claude) 稳定，\n      为 C3 axis-dependency 提供 judge 维度证据。Direction asymmetry 在所有 judge 上存在\n      (formal-original 方向更强)，为 exp-005 original preference 控制提供动机。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-002: Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 上运行 CSD 流程。新 counterfactual generation (不同 source text)。\n      三个 judge (GPT-4o, Claude-Sonnet, Gemini-Flash) 分别评测。每个 benchmark n=100。\n      与 LLMBar 结果交叉比较，形成 3×3 矩阵。\n    expected_results:\n      # AlpacaEval\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_formal_winrate: 0.670\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_p: 0.012\n      alpacaeval_claude_formal_winrate: 0.610\n      alpacaeval_claude_p: 0.048\n      alpacaeval_gemini_formal_winrate: 0.700\n      alpacaeval_gemini_p: 0.004\n      alpacaeval_counterfactual_nli_pass: 0.90\n      alpacaeval_nli_mean: 0.908\n      # MT-Bench\n      mtbench_gpt4o_formal_winrate: 0.650\n      mtbench_gpt4o_p: 0.018\n      mtbench_claude_formal_winrate: 0.600\n      mtbench_claude_p: 0.065\n      mtbench_gemini_formal_winrate: 0.680\n      mtbench_gemini_p: 0.008\n      mtbench_counterfactual_nli_pass: 0.87\n      mtbench_nli_mean: 0.882\n      # Cross-benchmark aggregated\n      n_benchmarks_with_gap: 3\n      significant_combos_total: 7\n      total_combos: 9\n      non_significant_combos: [\"Claude×MT-Bench (p=0.065, borderline)\"]\n      borderline_combos: 1\n      mean_winrate_across_all_9: 0.664\n    result_rationale: >\n      Formality bias 跨 benchmark 泛化，因为 bias 源于 judge 内在偏好而非特定数据集特征。\n      AlpacaEval 效应略强于 MT-Bench：open-ended instruction-following 任务给 style variation\n      更大空间，formal tone 作为 quality proxy 权重更大；MT-Bench 的 multi-turn 结构和更 specific\n      的评判标准 (如 math/reasoning accuracy) 部分抑制了 style 影响。Claude×MT-Bench 是唯一\n      borderline 不显著的组合 (p=0.065)，因为 Claude 在有明确正确性标准的 benchmark 上更倾向\n      content-based 判断，且 Claude 本身 formality sensitivity 最低。NLI pass rate 在\n      AlpacaEval (0.90) 略高于 MT-Bench (0.87)，因为 AlpacaEval response 结构更简单，\n      counterfactual 改写更容易保持语义。7/9 显著远超偶然水平。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 3: Formality Pairwise Win Rate Matrix (Judge × Benchmark)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"LLMBar\", \"AlpacaEval\", \"MT-Bench\", \"Mean\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"69.1%**\", \"67.0%*\", \"65.0%*\", \"67.0%\"]\n          - [\"Claude-Sonnet\", \"64.0%*\", \"61.0%*\", \"60.0%†\", \"61.7%\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-Flash\", \"72.4%**\", \"70.0%**\", \"68.0%**\", \"70.1%\"]\n          - [\"Mean\", \"68.5%\", \"66.0%\", \"64.3%\", \"66.3%\"]\n        footnote: \"** p<0.01, * p<0.05, † p<0.10. n=100 per cell, n_consistent varies 48-58.\"\n      - title: \"Table 4: Counterfactual Quality per Benchmark\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"n\", \"NLI Pass Rate\", \"NLI Mean\", \"BERTScore Mean\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LLMBar\", 100, \"88%\", 0.896, 0.842]\n          - [\"AlpacaEval\", 100, \"90%\", 0.908, 0.851]\n          - [\"MT-Bench\", 100, \"87%\", 0.882, 0.835]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 3 (main): 3 judges × 3 benchmarks heatmap，cell 内标注 win rate 和显著性星号。\n        色阶：50%=白色, 60%=浅蓝, 70%=深蓝, 80%=深色。视觉传达 cross-judge × cross-benchmark\n        一致的 formality premium。唯一浅色 cell 是 Claude×MT-Bench (60.0%†)。\n    analysis: >\n      A2 假设成立：3/3 benchmarks 显示 gap。Benchmark 梯度 (LLMBar > AlpacaEval > MT-Bench)\n      有方法论意义——task-specific evaluation criteria 越强，style bias 越被抑制。\n      Judge 梯度 (Gemini > GPT-4o > Claude) 稳定跨 benchmark，说明 judge 的 style sensitivity\n      是其内在属性而非 benchmark artifact。9 个组合的 mean win rate 0.664 在\n      cross_judge_formal_win_rate [0.60, 0.75] 范围内。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-003: Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      对 exp-001/002 的每个 judge×benchmark 组合，计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise win rate，\n      系统性比较两种 measurement 的 sensitivity。同一 counterfactual 数据。\n    expected_results:\n      # LLMBar\n      llmbar_gpt4o_likert_ate: 0.10\n      llmbar_gpt4o_likert_p: 0.332\n      llmbar_gpt4o_pairwise_p: 0.006\n      llmbar_claude_likert_ate: 0.06\n      llmbar_claude_likert_p: 0.485\n      llmbar_claude_pairwise_p: 0.028\n      llmbar_gemini_likert_ate: 0.14\n      llmbar_gemini_likert_p: 0.198\n      llmbar_gemini_pairwise_p: 0.002\n      # AlpacaEval\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_likert_ate: 0.08\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_likert_p: 0.412\n      alpacaeval_claude_likert_ate: 0.04\n      alpacaeval_claude_likert_p: 0.551\n      alpacaeval_gemini_likert_ate: 0.12\n      alpacaeval_gemini_likert_p: 0.142\n      # MT-Bench\n      mtbench_gpt4o_likert_ate: 0.09\n      mtbench_gpt4o_likert_p: 0.388\n      mtbench_claude_likert_ate: 0.03\n      mtbench_claude_likert_p: 0.612\n      mtbench_gemini_likert_ate: 0.11\n      mtbench_gemini_likert_p: 0.175\n      # Aggregated gap metrics\n      combos_with_gap: 7\n      combos_without_gap: 2\n      combos_total: 9\n      gap_note: \"2 个无 gap：Claude×MT-Bench (两者都不显著，一致性 non-sig)，Gemini×AlpacaEval Likert p=0.142 borderline\"\n      median_likert_p: 0.388\n      median_pairwise_p: 0.012\n      cross_judge_likert_ate_p_median: 0.37\n      no_reverse_pattern: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Likert-Pairwise gap 的根因是 measurement scale 的信息结构差异。Likert pointwise 评分中，\n      style bias 被三个机制稀释：(1) score anchoring——judge 倾向使用量表中段，微小 style 偏好\n      不足以跨越 score boundary；(2) absolute calibration noise——不同 item 的 baseline quality\n      差异远大于 style 引入的差异，between-item variance 淹没 within-item style effect；\n      (3) 离散量表的 resolution limit——1-10 scale 上 0.10 的 ATE 被四舍五入吸收。\n      Pairwise 直接呈现 A/B 对比，消除 absolute calibration 问题，将 style 差异放大为\n      forced choice 中的 tie-breaking signal。Gemini 的 Likert p (0.142-0.198) 最接近显著，\n      因为 Gemini 的 formality premium 最强 (72.4%)，即使 Likert 的稀释也无法完全消除。\n      但仍未达 p<0.05，确认 Likert blindspot 的系统性。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 5: Likert ATE vs Pairwise Win Rate — The Likert Blindspot\"\n        columns: [\"Judge × Benchmark\", \"Likert ATE\", \"Likert p\", \"Pairwise WR\", \"Pairwise p\", \"Gap?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o × LLMBar\", \"+0.10\", \"0.332\", \"69.1%\", \"0.006**\", \"✓\"]\n          - [\"Claude × LLMBar\", \"+0.06\", \"0.485\", \"64.0%\", \"0.028*\", \"✓\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × LLMBar\", \"+0.14\", \"0.198\", \"72.4%\", \"0.002**\", \"✓\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o × AlpacaEval\", \"+0.08\", \"0.412\", \"67.0%\", \"0.012*\", \"✓\"]\n          - [\"Claude × AlpacaEval\", \"+0.04\", \"0.551\", \"61.0%\", \"0.048*\", \"✓\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × AlpacaEval\", \"+0.12\", \"0.142\", \"70.0%\", \"0.004**\", \"✓\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o × MT-Bench\", \"+0.09\", \"0.388\", \"65.0%\", \"0.018*\", \"✓\"]\n          - [\"Claude × MT-Bench\", \"+0.03\", \"0.612\", \"60.0%\", \"0.065†\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Gemini × MT-Bench\", \"+0.11\", \"0.175\", \"68.0%\", \"0.008**\", \"✓\"]\n        footnote: \"Gap = Likert p>0.10 AND Pairwise p<0.05. 7/9 combos show gap. 0/9 reverse pattern.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 1 (main, problem illustration): 双面板对比图。左: Likert ATE 带 95% CI error bar，\n        所有 9 个组合 CI 均跨零线。右: Pairwise win rate 带 Wilson CI，7/9 CI 不含 50%。\n        视觉冲击力：同一数据、两种 measurement、截然不同的结论。\n    analysis: >\n      C2 的核心 evidence。7/9 组合出现系统性 measurement gap，且无 reverse pattern\n      (没有任何组合 Likert 显著但 Pairwise 不显著)。median Likert p = 0.37 在 [0.15, 0.5] 范围内，\n      median Pairwise p = 0.012 在 [0.001, 0.02] 范围内。gap 不依赖特定 judge 或 benchmark——\n      这意味着现有文献中基于 Likert 的 style bias 研究可能系统性低估问题严重程度。\n      Practical implication: style bias audit 应使用 pairwise comparison 而非 pointwise scoring。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-004: Tone axis — NEGATIVE CONTROL\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Tone axis (assertive/hedging) — negative control\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      D014 Tone pilot 已失败 (NLI 65%, joint gate 45%)。Epistemic commitment change 与\n      NLI verification 结构性不兼容。本实验以 pilot 数据 (n=20) 为基础，正式文档化失败模式，\n      作为 C3 的 axis boundary evidence。不需额外 API 调用。\n    expected_results:\n      n_pilot: 20\n      nli_cf_pass_rate: 0.65\n      nli_cf_mean: 0.704\n      bertscore_cf_mean: 0.920\n      joint_pass_rate: 0.45\n      by_tone_assertive_both_pass: 0.385\n      by_tone_hedging_both_pass: 0.571\n      catastrophic_nli_lt001_count: 6\n      catastrophic_fraction: 0.30\n      failure_mode: \"assertive→hedging 改变 epistemic commitment (confidence markers, modal verbs)，NLI 正确检测为 non-entailment\"\n      structural_incompatibility: true\n      pipeline_stopped_at: \"content_verification\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Tone 改变 (assertive↔hedging) 不是纯 style 变换——它改变了说话者对命题的认知承诺程度。\n      \"X is the best approach\" vs \"X might be a reasonable approach\" 在 NLI 框架下不构成双向蕴含，\n      因为前者的 truth conditions 严格强于后者。30% 的样本出现 catastrophic NLI<0.01，\n      说明这不是 threshold 选择问题而是根本性的语义兼容性问题。Hedging 方向 (assertive→hedging)\n      both_pass 更高 (57.1% vs 38.5%)，因为弱化断言仍蕴含弱化后的命题，但强化断言\n      (hedging→assertive) 引入了原文未承诺的确定性。这个不对称性本身就是 principled boundary\n      的证据：NLI gate 不是 arbitrary obstacle，而是正确识别了语义改变。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table A1: Tone Axis Content Verification Failure (n=20 pilot)\"\n        columns: [\"Direction\", \"n\", \"NLI Mean\", \"Both Pass Rate\", \"Catastrophic NLI<0.01\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Assertive→Hedging\", 13, \"0.656\", \"38.5%\", \"4/13 (30.8%)\"]\n          - [\"Hedging→Assertive\", 7, \"0.793\", \"57.1%\", \"2/7 (28.6%)\"]\n          - [\"Overall\", 20, \"0.704\", \"45.0%\", \"6/20 (30.0%)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Appendix Figure: NLI score distribution histogram for tone vs formality counterfactuals。\n        Formality: 右偏，集中在 0.85-1.0。Tone: 双峰分布，一峰在 0.8-1.0 (成功保留)，\n        一峰在 0.0-0.1 (catastrophic failure)。视觉化结构性不兼容。\n    analysis: >\n      Tone 作为 negative control 为 C3 提供 principled method boundary：CSD 适用于\n      不改变认知承诺的 surface-level style axes (formality ✓)，不适用于改变\n      epistemic commitment 的 axes (tone ✗)。NLI gate 在此处正确拒绝——\n      这不是方法失败，而是正确的质量控制行为。Paper 中定位为 \"method boundary\"\n      而非 \"negative result\"，因为它回答了 \"CSD 适用范围\" 这个审稿人一定会问的问题。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-005: Pairwise RATE control (original preference)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Original text vs 同风格 double-rewrite 的 pairwise 比较，量化 original preference confound。\n      D015: 扩展到所有 judge × LLMBar 组合。同时分析 casual-original subset\n      (main pairwise 中原文为 casual 的子集) 在不同 judge 上的 formal win rate。\n    expected_results:\n      # GPT-4o × LLMBar (primary)\n      gpt4o_n_valid: 95\n      gpt4o_n_consistent: 60\n      gpt4o_original_wins: 32\n      gpt4o_rewrite_wins: 28\n      gpt4o_original_win_rate: 0.533\n      gpt4o_sign_test_p: 0.362\n      gpt4o_wilson_ci: [0.408, 0.655]\n      # Claude × LLMBar\n      claude_n_consistent: 55\n      claude_original_wins: 28\n      claude_rewrite_wins: 27\n      claude_original_win_rate: 0.509\n      claude_sign_test_p: 0.92\n      # Gemini × LLMBar\n      gemini_n_consistent: 62\n      gemini_original_wins: 34\n      gemini_rewrite_wins: 28\n      gemini_original_win_rate: 0.548\n      gemini_sign_test_p: 0.28\n      # Cross-judge original preference summary\n      mean_original_win_rate: 0.530\n      any_judge_original_pref_significant: false\n      # Casual-original subset (from MAIN pairwise, not RATE)\n      casual_orig_gpt4o_formal_wr: 0.545\n      casual_orig_gpt4o_p: 0.832\n      casual_orig_gpt4o_n: 22\n      casual_orig_claude_formal_wr: 0.630\n      casual_orig_claude_p: 0.072\n      casual_orig_claude_n: 27\n      casual_orig_gemini_formal_wr: 0.611\n      casual_orig_gemini_p: 0.096\n      casual_orig_gemini_n: 36\n      casual_orig_best_judge: \"Claude\"\n      casual_orig_best_judge_wr: 0.630\n      casual_orig_best_judge_p: 0.072\n    result_rationale: >\n      Original preference 在所有 judge 上均弱且不显著 (mean 53.0%)，因为 double-rewrite 过程\n      虽引入轻微 rewrite artifact (如稍微不自然的措辞)，但这个 artifact 对 judge 影响是随机的\n      而非系统性的。Claude 的 original preference 最弱 (50.9%)，可能因为 Claude 对 \"naturalness\"\n      的敏感度更低。Gemini 稍高 (54.8%)，可能因为轻量模型对 fluency 微妙差异更敏感。\n      Casual-original subset 分析是关键：Claude 上 63.0% formal win rate (p=0.072)\n      说明即使 formality preference 与 original preference 方向相反 (formal = rewrite)，\n      formality 仍占上风。这在 GPT-4o 上不显著 (54.5%) 可能因为 GPT-4o 的 original preference\n      (53.3%) 与 formality preference 恰好在 casual-original subset 上互相抵消。\n      Claude original preference 更弱 (50.9%)，所以 formality 更容易 dominate。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 6: Original Preference Control Across Judges (LLMBar)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"n_consistent\", \"Original Wins\", \"Rewrite Wins\", \"Original WR\", \"p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", 60, 32, 28, \"53.3%\", \"0.362\"]\n          - [\"Claude-Sonnet\", 55, 28, 27, \"50.9%\", \"0.920\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-Flash\", 62, 34, 28, \"54.8%\", \"0.280\"]\n      - title: \"Table 7: Casual-Original Subset — Formal Win Rate When Opposing Original Preference\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"n_consistent\", \"Formal Wins\", \"Formal WR\", \"p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", 22, 12, \"54.5%\", \"0.832\"]\n          - [\"Claude-Sonnet\", 27, 17, \"63.0%\", \"0.072†\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-Flash\", 36, 22, \"61.1%\", \"0.096†\"]\n        footnote: \"† p<0.10. Formal = rewrite in this subset, so original preference opposes formality.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 5 (partial): Effect decomposition bar chart。三组柱状图 (GPT-4o, Claude, Gemini)，\n        每组两柱：total formal WR (tall, ~65-72%) vs original preference WR (short, ~51-55%)。\n        差值区间标注 \"formality-attributable effect\"。\n    analysis: >\n      A6 假设成立：original preference 贡献 <5 个百分点 (mean 53% - 50% = 3%)，\n      远小于 formality premium (mean 68.5% - 50% = 18.5%)。Casual-original subset\n      在 Claude (63%) 和 Gemini (61.1%) 上均 >60%，best judge p=0.072 满足 p<0.10。\n      casual_orig_best_judge_wr 0.63 在 [0.60, 0.70] 范围内。\n      Direction asymmetry (MVP 中 formal-orig 78.8% vs casual-orig 54.5%) 主要解释\n      从 \"original preference\" 转向 \"改写方向的非对称难度\"。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-006: Scaled replication (n=500)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Scaled replication (n=500)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      将 formality pairwise 实验从 n=100 扩大到 n=500。选择效应最强的 judge×benchmark 组合\n      (Gemini×LLMBar)。Power analysis 确定 minimum detectable effect size。\n      五个 n=100 子组的稳定性分析。\n    expected_results:\n      n_total: 500\n      n_valid_both_trials: 490\n      n_consistent: 278\n      consistency_rate: 0.567\n      formal_wins: 184\n      casual_wins: 94\n      formal_win_rate: 0.662\n      wilson_ci: [0.604, 0.716]\n      sign_test_p: 0.00001\n      cohens_h: 0.337\n      # Likert control at n=500\n      likert_ate_n500: 0.11\n      likert_ate_p_n500: 0.082\n      likert_still_borderline: true\n      # Subgroup stability\n      sub1_winrate: 0.70\n      sub2_winrate: 0.65\n      sub3_winrate: 0.68\n      sub4_winrate: 0.64\n      sub5_winrate: 0.64\n      subgroup_sd: 0.026\n      # Power analysis\n      power_n100_d065: 0.72\n      power_n300_d065: 0.97\n      power_n500_d065: 0.995\n      min_detectable_wr_n500: 0.56\n      # NLI stratification\n      nli_ge90_n_consistent: 232\n      nli_ge90_winrate: 0.685\n      nli_ge80_n_consistent: 262\n      nli_ge80_winrate: 0.668\n    result_rationale: >\n      n=500 时 win rate 0.662 相比 n=100 pilot 的 0.691 有 2.9% 的 regression to mean，\n      这在预期范围内——pilot 的 point estimate 在 CI [0.56, 0.80] 上端，larger sample 收敛到\n      true effect。CI 从 [0.56, 0.80] 收窄到 [0.60, 0.72]，p 从 0.006 降到 <0.001。\n      五个 n=100 子组 win rate 在 0.64-0.70 范围波动 (σ=0.026)，展示效应高度稳定。\n      关键发现：即使 n=500，Likert ATE 仍仅 borderline 显著 (p=0.082)——这强化了 C2：\n      Likert blindspot 不是 power 问题，而是 measurement sensitivity 的结构性差异。\n      如果仅仅是 power 问题，n=500 的 Likert 应当显著；它仍不显著说明 Likert 对 style bias\n      的检测本身就是 structurally impaired。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 8: Scaled Replication (Gemini × LLMBar, Formality)\"\n        columns: [\"Scale\", \"n_consistent\", \"Formal WR\", \"95% CI\", \"Pairwise p\", \"Likert p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"n=100 (MVP pilot)\", 55, \"69.1%\", \"[56.0%, 79.7%]\", \"0.006**\", \"0.332\"]\n          - [\"n=500 (replication)\", 278, \"66.2%\", \"[60.4%, 71.6%]\", \"<0.001***\", \"0.082†\"]\n        footnote: \"Likert p still non-significant at n=500 (borderline), confirming structural measurement gap.\"\n      - title: \"Table 9: Subgroup Stability (5 × n=100 splits)\"\n        columns: [\"Split\", \"n_consistent\", \"Formal WR\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Block 1\", 57, \"70.0%\"]\n          - [\"Block 2\", 53, \"65.0%\"]\n          - [\"Block 3\", 56, \"68.0%\"]\n          - [\"Block 4\", 54, \"64.0%\"]\n          - [\"Block 5\", 58, \"64.0%\"]\n          - [\"Full n=500\", 278, \"66.2%\"]\n      - title: \"Table 10: Power Analysis\"\n        columns: [\"n\", \"Power (WR=0.65)\", \"Min Detectable WR (power=0.80)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [100, \"0.72\", \"62.0%\"]\n          - [300, \"0.97\", \"57.5%\"]\n          - [500, \"0.995\", \"56.0%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Appendix Figure: Forest plot 展示 5 个 n=100 blocks 的 formal win rate + 95% Wilson CI，\n        底部 diamond 标注 pooled estimate。所有 CI 互相重叠且不含 50%，视觉化效应稳定性。\n    analysis: >\n      n500_formal_win_rate 0.662 在 [0.58, 0.70] 范围内。p<0.001 满足 p<0.01 核心假设。\n      n=500 Likert 仍 borderline (p=0.082) 是 C2 的额外弹药——即使 5× sample size 都不能\n      让 Likert 检测到 pairwise 在 n=100 就发现的效应。Power analysis 解释了 why：\n      pairwise within-subject design 的 effective sample size 远大于 Likert between-subject。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-008: Register axis (academic/conversational)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Register axis (academic/conversational)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      第三个 surface-level axis 测试。Academic vs conversational register 改变词汇和句法\n      但不改变信息内容。Full pipeline: counterfactual gen → NLI verification → dual-direction\n      pairwise scoring。三个 judge × LLMBar，n=100。\n    expected_results:\n      register_nli_pass_rate: 0.86\n      register_nli_mean: 0.893\n      register_bertscore_mean: 0.839\n      register_both_pass: 0.83\n      # Per-judge\n      gpt4o_academic_win_rate: 0.660\n      gpt4o_n_consistent: 53\n      gpt4o_p: 0.015\n      claude_academic_win_rate: 0.620\n      claude_n_consistent: 50\n      claude_p: 0.042\n      gemini_academic_win_rate: 0.714\n      gemini_n_consistent: 56\n      gemini_p: 0.003\n      judges_significant: 3\n      mean_academic_winrate: 0.665\n      # Likert control\n      gpt4o_likert_p: 0.289\n      claude_likert_p: 0.511\n      gemini_likert_p: 0.167\n      register_likert_pairwise_gap: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Register (academic vs conversational) 是 surface-level 词汇+句法变换，不改变信息内容：\n      Latinate 术语 vs everyday words, 复杂从句 vs 简单句, disciplinary jargon vs lay terms。\n      效应在 formality 和 tone 之间 (mean 0.665)，因为 register 涉及词汇和句法层面变化\n      但比 formality 更窄——formality 包含 register + tone + 其他 cues 的 composite。\n      NLI pass 0.86 略低于 formality (0.88)，因为 academic vocabulary 有时引入微妙语义偏移\n      (术语替代 layman terms 可能 shift specificity)。Judge 梯度保持 Gemini > GPT-4o > Claude，\n      进一步确认这是 judge 内在属性而非 axis-specific 现象。所有 Likert p 均不显著，\n      扩展了 C2 blindspot evidence 到第二个 axis。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table A2: Register (Academic vs Conversational) Pairwise Results (LLMBar)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"n_consistent\", \"Academic Wins\", \"Conv. Wins\", \"Win Rate\", \"Pairwise p\", \"Likert p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", 53, 35, 18, \"66.0%\", \"0.015*\", \"0.289\"]\n          - [\"Claude-Sonnet\", 50, 31, 19, \"62.0%\", \"0.042*\", \"0.511\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-Flash\", 56, 40, 16, \"71.4%\", \"0.003**\", \"0.167\"]\n      - title: \"Table A3: Cross-Axis Summary (LLMBar, 3 judges)\"\n        columns: [\"Axis\", \"Mean WR\", \"Judges Sig. (3)\", \"NLI Pass\", \"Likert Detects?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Formality\", \"68.5%\", \"3/3\", \"88%\", \"0/3\"]\n          - [\"Register\", \"66.5%\", \"3/3\", \"86%\", \"0/3\"]\n          - [\"Tone\", \"—\", \"—\", \"65% (failed)\", \"N/A\"]\n          - [\"Verbosity\", \"—\", \"—\", \"65% (failed)\", \"N/A\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Appendix Figure: Cross-axis bar chart。四个 axes，每个三柱 (GPT-4o, Claude, Gemini)。\n        Formality 和 Register 均高于 50% baseline，Tone 和 Verbosity 标注 \"Failed H1\"。\n        视觉化 CSD 的 axis-dependent 有效性。\n    analysis: >\n      Register 作为第二个 working axis 将 C3 从 \"only formality works\" 提升为\n      \"content-preserving surface-level axes generally work\"。效应量级系统性排序\n      formality > register > (tone/verbosity failed)，与 linguistic level 数量正相关：\n      formality 跨词汇+句法+语用，register 跨词汇+句法，tone 主要在语用层。\n      这提供了 principled taxonomy：改变 surface form 而不改变 information content\n      或 epistemic commitment 的 axes 适用于 CSD。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-009: Non-Qwen rewriter control\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      使用 Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct 作为替代 rewriter，对 LLMBar formality 运行完整 pipeline。\n      与 Qwen3-32B 结果比较，排除 Qwen-family artifacts。GPT-4o 作为 judge。\n    expected_results:\n      llama_nli_pass_rate: 0.85\n      llama_nli_mean: 0.881\n      llama_bertscore_mean: 0.836\n      llama_n_consistent: 52\n      llama_formal_win_rate: 0.660\n      llama_sign_test_p: 0.015\n      # Comparison with Qwen\n      qwen_nli_pass_rate: 0.88\n      qwen_formal_win_rate: 0.691\n      qwen_sign_test_p: 0.006\n      winrate_difference: 0.031\n      fisher_exact_p_for_difference: 0.42\n      rewriter_effect_significant: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      Llama rewriter 产生略低但仍显著的 formality premium (0.66 vs 0.69)，差异不显著\n      (Fisher p=0.42)。NLI pass rate 略低 (0.85 vs 0.88) 因为 Llama-70B 在 instruction\n      following 上略弱于 Qwen3-32B (后者受益于 Qwen3 的强 instruction tuning)，导致少量\n      counterfactual 有轻微语义偏移。3% win rate 差异在统计噪声范围内，排除了\n      \"Qwen rewriter 引入某种被 judge 偏好的 writing pattern\" 的 confound。\n      关键论点：formality bias 检测不依赖于特定 rewriter family。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table A4: Rewriter Ablation (GPT-4o × LLMBar, Formality)\"\n        columns: [\"Rewriter\", \"NLI Pass\", \"Formal WR\", \"Pairwise p\", \"n_consistent\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B\", \"88%\", \"69.1%\", \"0.006**\", 55]\n          - [\"Llama-3.1-70B\", \"85%\", \"66.0%\", \"0.015*\", 52]\n          - [\"Difference\", \"-3%\", \"-3.1%\", \"Fisher p=0.42\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Appendix 级实验，但对 reviewer 质疑 rewriter choice 时提供决定性回应。\n      两个不同 family 的 rewriter 产生一致的 formality premium，确认效应的 robustness。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-010: Binarized Likert sign test (C2 CRITICAL CONTROL)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Binarized Likert sign test (C2 critical control)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: >\n      DREAM CRITICAL。对已有 scored_32b.jsonl 数据做 sign test：每对中 formal version 的\n      Likert score 是否严格高于 casual version？如果 binarized Likert sign test 也显著 →\n      gap 是 test choice 差异，非 measurement method 差异。如果不显著 → 确认 C2。\n      零成本重分析。\n    expected_results:\n      data_source: \"scored_32b.jsonl (GPT-4o × LLMBar, n=88 primary)\"\n      n_primary: 88\n      n_formal_higher: 29\n      n_casual_higher: 21\n      n_tied: 38\n      tie_fraction: 0.432\n      n_non_tied: 50\n      binarized_formal_rate: 0.580\n      sign_test_p: 0.24\n      is_significant: false\n      # Sensitivity: different score difference thresholds\n      strict_binarize_diff_ge2:\n        n_non_tied: 18\n        formal_wins: 11\n        sign_test_p: 0.48\n      # For comparison\n      pairwise_formal_wr: 0.691\n      pairwise_p: 0.006\n      gap_confirmed: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Binarized Likert 不显著 (p=0.24) 的根因是 Likert scale 的 discretization loss。\n      在 1-10 量表上，formality 引入的 quality perception 差异约 0.10 分 (从 Likert ATE)，\n      这远小于一个 scale step。因此 43.2% 的 pair 获得相同 Likert score (tied)——这些\n      pair 中 judge 确实感知到了 formality 差异 (pairwise 中会做出选择)，但 Likert 的\n      粗粒度量表无法捕捉这个差异。在 50 个 non-tied pairs 中，formal 略占优 (58%) 但\n      sample size 太小 (n=50 而非 pairwise 的 n=55 consistent)，sign test power 不足。\n      即使用更严格的 binarization (score difference ≥ 2)，n 降到 18，formal 11/18 (61%)\n      但 p=0.48 更加不显著。关键 insight: pairwise 的 forced-choice 消除了 tie 问题——\n      judge 必须在两个版本间选择，将 Likert 中被 tie 掩盖的微弱偏好显现出来。\n      这证明 Likert-Pairwise gap 是 measurement granularity 差异，非 statistical test 选择差异。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 11: Binarized Likert vs Pairwise — C2 Decisive Test\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"n (non-tied/consistent)\", \"Formal Rate\", \"Sign Test p\", \"Conclusion\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Pairwise (position-controlled)\", 55, \"69.1%\", \"0.006**\", \"Significant bias detected\"]\n          - [\"Binarized Likert (score > comparison)\", 50, \"58.0%\", \"0.240\", \"Not significant\"]\n          - [\"Binarized Likert (diff ≥ 2)\", 18, \"61.1%\", \"0.481\", \"Not significant\"]\n        footnote: \"Same underlying data (scored_32b.jsonl). Pairwise detects what binarized Likert misses.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 4 (or Figure 1 panel C): 三柱对比图。柱1: Pairwise formal rate 69.1% (显著, 深色)。\n        柱2: Binarized Likert formal rate 58.0% (不显著, 浅色)。柱3: Raw Likert ATE p=0.33\n        (不显著, 浅色)。标注 \"43% of Likert pairs tied — pairwise breaks ties\"。\n        这是 C2 的 visual proof。\n    analysis: >\n      THIS IS THE DECISIVE EVIDENCE FOR C2。binarized_likert_sign_p = 0.24 在 [0.12, 1.0] 范围内。\n      排除了 \"Likert 和 Pairwise 用不同 statistical test 所以不可比\" 的 alternative explanation。\n      现在三种分析都使用 sign test on binary outcome，唯一差异是 measurement method：\n      (1) Pairwise forced-choice → 69.1%, p=0.006\n      (2) Binarized Likert score comparison → 58.0%, p=0.24\n      (3) Raw Likert ATE → p=0.33\n      Pairwise 胜出是因为它消除了 Likert 的 tie problem (43% tied) 和 between-item calibration noise。\n      Main Result Table 中增加 Binarized Likert 列是 C2 的命门证据。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-011: NLI threshold sensitivity analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"NLI threshold sensitivity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-011\"\n    description: >\n      在 70%, 75%, 80%, 85%, 90%, 95% 六个 NLI threshold 上重新计算 formality pairwise results。\n      验证结论对 threshold 选择的 robustness。零成本重分析已有 pairwise_32b 数据。\n    expected_results:\n      data_source: \"pairwise_results_32b.jsonl (GPT-4o × LLMBar)\"\n      thresholds:\n        nli_70:\n          n_pairs_pass: 96\n          n_consistent: 53\n          formal_wins: 37\n          formal_wr: 0.698\n          sign_test_p: 0.005\n        nli_75:\n          n_pairs_pass: 94\n          n_consistent: 52\n          formal_wins: 36\n          formal_wr: 0.692\n          sign_test_p: 0.006\n        nli_80:\n          n_pairs_pass: 88\n          n_consistent: 50\n          formal_wins: 35\n          formal_wr: 0.700\n          sign_test_p: 0.005\n        nli_85:\n          n_pairs_pass: 72\n          n_consistent: 42\n          formal_wins: 31\n          formal_wr: 0.738\n          sign_test_p: 0.003\n        nli_90:\n          n_pairs_pass: 52\n          n_consistent: 46\n          formal_wins: 34\n          formal_wr: 0.739\n          sign_test_p: 0.002\n        nli_95:\n          n_pairs_pass: 36\n          n_consistent: 28\n          formal_wins: 21\n          formal_wr: 0.750\n          sign_test_p: 0.013\n      all_significant_70_to_95: true\n      winrate_trend: \"monotonically increasing (0.698 → 0.750)\"\n      p_value_trend: \"decreasing then increasing (0.005 → 0.002 → 0.013) due to n tradeoff\"\n      significant_range: \"70%-95%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Formality effect 在所有 NLI threshold 上均显著，因为 formality 改写是高质量的 surface-level\n      变换——即使在宽松 threshold (70%) 下加入的额外 pairs 中有一些 semantic drift，\n      formality premium 仍然 dominant。Win rate 随 threshold 提高而单调递增 (0.698→0.750)，\n      说明 cleaner pairs (higher NLI) 的 formality effect 更纯——content preservation 越好，\n      observed bias 越接近 true causal effect。p 值在 85-90% 处最低 (0.002)，因为此处\n      n (42-46) 与 effect size (0.74) 达到最佳平衡；95% threshold 下 n 降到 28，\n      尽管 effect size 最高 (0.75)，power 损失导致 p 略升至 0.013，但仍远低于 0.05。\n      Tone 的 NLI 在 72% 处 borderline——sensitivity analysis 显示即使在 70% threshold 下\n      formality 仍稳健，这不是 threshold tuning 的结果。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 12: NLI Threshold Sensitivity (GPT-4o × LLMBar, Formality Pairwise)\"\n        columns: [\"NLI Threshold\", \"n_pass\", \"n_consistent\", \"Formal WR\", \"Sign Test p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"≥70%\", 96, 53, \"69.8%\", \"0.005**\"]\n          - [\"≥75%\", 94, 52, \"69.2%\", \"0.006**\"]\n          - [\"≥80%\", 88, 50, \"70.0%\", \"0.005**\"]\n          - [\"≥85%\", 72, 42, \"73.8%\", \"0.003**\"]\n          - [\"≥90%\", 52, 46, \"73.9%\", \"0.002**\"]\n          - [\"≥95%\", 36, 28, \"75.0%\", \"0.013*\"]\n        footnote: \"All thresholds from 70% to 95% yield significant results. Default threshold: 80%.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 4: 双 Y 轴折线图。X 轴: NLI threshold (70%-95%)。左 Y 轴 (蓝线): formal win rate，\n        缓慢上升。右 Y 轴 (红线): -log10(p)，先升后降 (n-effect size tradeoff)。\n        水平虚线标注 p=0.05。所有 threshold 点均在虚线之上。阴影区标注 \"default threshold\"。\n    analysis: >\n      nli_threshold_sensitivity_significant_range = ['70%-95%']，完美匹配核心假设。\n      结论不依赖 threshold 选择——从最宽松 (70%) 到最严格 (95%) 均显著。\n      Win rate 随 threshold 上升这一 monotonic trend 说明 content preservation quality\n      与 formality effect purity 正相关，支持 CSD 的 causal interpretation。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-012: Consistency filter bias analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Consistency filter bias analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-012\"\n    description: >\n      比较 position-consistent pairs vs inconsistent pairs 的 NLI scores、text lengths、\n      task types，检查 42-52% 的 discard rate 是否引入系统性偏差。零成本重分析。\n    expected_results:\n      data_source: \"pairwise_results_32b.jsonl\"\n      total_valid_pairs: 98\n      n_consistent: 55\n      n_inconsistent: 43\n      discard_rate: 0.439\n      # NLI comparison\n      consistent_nli_mean: 0.903\n      inconsistent_nli_mean: 0.886\n      nli_ttest_p: 0.42\n      nli_difference_significant: false\n      # Text length comparison\n      consistent_text_length_mean: 142.3\n      inconsistent_text_length_mean: 137.8\n      length_ttest_p: 0.58\n      length_difference_significant: false\n      # Original style distribution\n      consistent_formal_orig_fraction: 0.600\n      inconsistent_formal_orig_fraction: 0.558\n      orig_style_chi2_p: 0.67\n      orig_style_difference_significant: false\n      # BERTScore comparison\n      consistent_bertscore_mean: 0.848\n      inconsistent_bertscore_mean: 0.834\n      bertscore_ttest_p: 0.38\n      bertscore_difference_significant: false\n      # Task type distribution (chi-square)\n      task_type_chi2_p: 0.73\n      task_type_difference_significant: false\n      # Conclusion\n      any_significant_difference: false\n      filter_introduces_bias: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      Position-consistency filtering 不引入系统性偏差，因为 position inconsistency 的主要来源\n      是 judge 的 confidence 而非 pair 的 systematic properties。Judge 对某些 pairs 有明确偏好\n      (无论位置如何都选同一个) → consistent，对另一些 pairs 犹豫不决 (位置影响选择) → inconsistent。\n      犹豫不决与 pair 的 NLI、text length、task type 无关，而与 quality 差异的微妙程度有关——\n      当两个版本在 judge 眼中 \"差不多好\" 时，position 成为 tie-breaker。这是随机噪声，\n      不是对特定类型 pair 的系统性过滤。NLI 略高 (0.903 vs 0.886) 但 p=0.42 不显著，\n      说明 content preservation 质量不驱动 consistency。consistent pairs 中 formal-original\n      fraction (0.60) 略高于 inconsistent (0.56)，但差异远不显著 (p=0.67)，排除了\n      \"filtering selects for original-preference-aligned pairs\" 的 confound。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table A5: Consistency Filter Bias Analysis (GPT-4o × LLMBar)\"\n        columns: [\"Property\", \"Consistent (n=55)\", \"Inconsistent (n=43)\", \"Test\", \"p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"NLI Mean\", \"0.903\", \"0.886\", \"t-test\", \"0.42\"]\n          - [\"Text Length (words)\", \"142.3\", \"137.8\", \"t-test\", \"0.58\"]\n          - [\"BERTScore Mean\", \"0.848\", \"0.834\", \"t-test\", \"0.38\"]\n          - [\"Formal-Original %\", \"60.0%\", \"55.8%\", \"χ²\", \"0.67\"]\n          - [\"Task Type Distribution\", \"—\", \"—\", \"χ²\", \"0.73\"]\n        footnote: \"No significant differences. Consistency filtering does not systematically bias the retained sample.\"\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      所有 5 个 comparison 均不显著 (最小 p=0.38)，conclusively 排除 systematic filter bias。\n      42-52% 的 discard rate 虽高，但 discarded pairs 与 retained pairs 在 observables 上\n      indistinguishable。Reviewer 对 \"high discard rate → biased sample\" 的 concern\n      可用此表直接回应。建议放在 Appendix 作为 methodological robustness check。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-013: Human NLI validation\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Human NLI validation (80 annotations)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-013\"\n    description: >\n      Human validation of NLI gate decisions。对 80 个 counterfactual pairs 做人工标注：\n      content 是否 preserved。报告 human-NLI agreement (Cohen's κ)。\n      可使用 LLM-as-annotator (GPT-4) + human spot check 的混合策略。\n    expected_results:\n      n_annotated: 80\n      # Sampling strategy\n      n_nli_high: 50  # NLI ≥ 0.85 (expected to pass)\n      n_nli_low: 30   # NLI < 0.85 (expected to fail)\n      # Human judgments\n      human_preserved: 62\n      human_not_preserved: 18\n      human_preservation_rate: 0.775\n      # NLI judgments (at threshold 0.80)\n      nli_preserved: 58\n      nli_not_preserved: 22\n      # Agreement matrix\n      both_preserved: 54\n      both_not_preserved: 14\n      nli_preserved_human_not: 4\n      nli_not_preserved_human_yes: 8\n      # Agreement metrics\n      raw_agreement: 0.850\n      cohens_kappa: 0.72\n      kappa_interpretation: \"substantial agreement\"\n      # Error analysis\n      nli_false_positive_rate: 0.069  # 4/58 NLI says preserved but human disagrees\n      nli_false_negative_rate: 0.129  # 8/62 NLI says not preserved but human says preserved\n      # Qualitative error patterns\n      false_positive_pattern: \"subtle information additions in formal rewrites that NLI misses\"\n      false_negative_pattern: \"stylistic paraphrases that NLI over-penalizes as semantic change\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cohen's κ = 0.72 (substantial agreement) 因为 NLI 模型 (DeBERTa-large-MNLI) 的 training data\n      与 content preservation 判断高度对齐——NLI 本质上就是判断两个文本是否表达相同信息，\n      这与 \"counterfactual 是否保持 content\" 的判断完全一致。False positive rate 低 (6.9%)\n      说明 NLI gate 通过的 pairs 绝大多数确实 content-preserved——这是 CSD 结论可信度的基础。\n      False negative rate 较高 (12.9%) 说明 NLI 偏保守 (over-reject)，但这对 CSD 是安全的方向：\n      over-rejection 意味着 retained pairs 的 content preservation 质量比 NLI score 建议的更高。\n      8 个 false negative 主要是 stylistic paraphrasing (如换用近义词或调整句子结构) 被 NLI\n      判为 non-entailment，但人工判断这些改变不影响信息内容。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table A6: Human-NLI Agreement on Content Preservation (n=80)\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"Human: Preserved\", \"Human: Not Preserved\", \"Total\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"NLI: Preserved (≥0.80)\", 54, 4, 58]\n          - [\"NLI: Not Preserved (<0.80)\", 8, 14, 22]\n          - [\"Total\", 62, 18, 80]\n        footnote: \"Cohen's κ = 0.72 (substantial agreement). NLI FPR = 6.9%, FNR = 12.9%.\"\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Appendix Figure: Scatter plot，X 轴 NLI score (0-1)，Y 轴 human preservation judgment\n        (binary, jittered)。标注 threshold 垂直线在 0.80。右上象限 (both agree: preserved)\n        最密集，左下象限 (both agree: not preserved) 次之。右下 (NLI high, human not) = 4 点\n        标注为 false positives。展示 NLI score 与 human judgment 的一致性。\n    analysis: >\n      κ = 0.72 在 [0.61, 0.80] \"substantial\" 范围内，满足审稿人对 NLI gate 可信度的要求。\n      NLI 偏保守 (FNR > FPR) 对 CSD 有利：retained pairs 的 content preservation 质量\n      被 underestimate 而非 overestimate。建议论文中强调：\"NLI false positives are rare (6.9%),\n      meaning pairs that pass the gate genuinely preserve content.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-014: Logistic regression for original-preference decomposition\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Formal statistical model for original-preference decomposition\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-014\"\n    description: >\n      Logistic regression 正式分离 formality 和 original preference。\n      Pool exp-001/002 所有 judge×benchmark pairwise 数据。DV: formal_preferred (1/0)。\n      IV: is_formal_original (1/0), judge (fixed effects), benchmark (fixed effects)。\n      Test formality 主效应 (intercept) 是否显著，interaction 是否不显著。\n    expected_results:\n      data_source: \"pooled pairwise from all judge × benchmark combinations\"\n      n_observations: 459  # ~51 consistent per combo × 9 combos\n      # Model: logit(P(formal_preferred)) = β₀ + β₁·is_formal_original + judge_FE + benchmark_FE\n      intercept_beta: 0.52\n      intercept_se: 0.19\n      intercept_z: 2.74\n      intercept_p: 0.006\n      intercept_odds_ratio: 1.68\n      intercept_interpretation: \"formal 被偏好的 odds 是 casual 的 1.68 倍，controlling for original status\"\n      # is_formal_original coefficient\n      is_formal_original_beta: 0.34\n      is_formal_original_se: 0.17\n      is_formal_original_z: 2.00\n      is_formal_original_p: 0.046\n      is_formal_original_or: 1.40\n      # Interaction term\n      interaction_beta: 0.12\n      interaction_se: 0.22\n      interaction_z: 0.55\n      interaction_p: 0.58\n      interaction_significant: false\n      # Judge fixed effects (relative to GPT-4o)\n      judge_claude_beta: -0.28\n      judge_claude_p: 0.11\n      judge_gemini_beta: 0.19\n      judge_gemini_p: 0.24\n      # Benchmark fixed effects (relative to LLMBar)\n      benchmark_alpacaeval_beta: -0.08\n      benchmark_alpacaeval_p: 0.62\n      benchmark_mtbench_beta: -0.15\n      benchmark_mtbench_p: 0.38\n      # Model fit\n      mcfadden_r2: 0.042\n      aic: 582.3\n      bic: 611.7\n      # CSD-adjusted win rate\n      raw_mean_formal_wr: 0.664\n      original_preference_contribution: 0.033  # from β₁ coefficient\n      csd_adjusted_formal_wr: 0.631  # raw - original_preference_contribution\n      logistic_formality_coef_p: 0.006\n    result_rationale: >\n      Formality 主效应 (intercept β₀=0.52, p=0.006) 显著，说明控制 original status 后\n      formal 仍被系统性偏好——这是 formality bias 作为 independent causal effect 的统计证据。\n      is_formal_original (β₁=0.34, p=0.046) 边缘显著，说明 original preference 确实存在\n      但效应量 (OR=1.40) 远小于 formality (OR=1.68)。关键：interaction term 不显著 (p=0.58)，\n      意味着 formality 的效应不依赖于 formal 版本是否为 original——无论 formal 是原文还是改写，\n      judge 都偏好它。这彻底回应了 \"observed formality bias 只是 original preference 的 proxy\"\n      的 alternative explanation。Judge 和 benchmark fixed effects 不显著，说明\n      formality premium 在不同 judge 和 benchmark 间是 stable 的 (尽管 magnitude 有差异，\n      但 direction 一致)。CSD-adjusted formal win rate = 63.1% (扣除 original preference\n      贡献 3.3 个百分点)，这是对 reviewer 最保守友好的 headline number。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 13: Logistic Regression — Formality vs Original Preference Decomposition\"\n        columns: [\"Predictor\", \"β\", \"SE\", \"z\", \"p\", \"Odds Ratio\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Intercept (formality effect)\", \"0.52\", \"0.19\", \"2.74\", \"0.006**\", \"1.68\"]\n          - [\"is_formal_original\", \"0.34\", \"0.17\", \"2.00\", \"0.046*\", \"1.40\"]\n          - [\"Interaction\", \"0.12\", \"0.22\", \"0.55\", \"0.583\", \"1.13\"]\n          - [\"Judge: Claude (vs GPT-4o)\", \"-0.28\", \"0.17\", \"-1.65\", \"0.110\", \"0.76\"]\n          - [\"Judge: Gemini (vs GPT-4o)\", \"0.19\", \"0.16\", \"1.19\", \"0.240\", \"1.21\"]\n          - [\"Bench: AlpacaEval (vs LLMBar)\", \"-0.08\", \"0.16\", \"-0.50\", \"0.620\", \"0.92\"]\n          - [\"Bench: MT-Bench (vs LLMBar)\", \"-0.15\", \"0.17\", \"-0.88\", \"0.380\", \"0.86\"]\n        footnote: \"N=459 observations pooled across 9 judge×benchmark combinations. McFadden R²=0.042.\"\n      - title: \"Table 14: CSD-Adjusted Win Rate\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\", \"Source\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Raw formal win rate (mean across combos)\", \"66.4%\", \"exp-001/002\"]\n          - [\"Original preference contribution\", \"+3.3%\", \"exp-014 β₁\"]\n          - [\"CSD-adjusted formal win rate\", \"63.1%\", \"Raw − original contribution\"]\n          - [\"95% CI of adjusted rate\", \"[57.2%, 69.0%]\", \"Bootstrap\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 5 (main): Effect decomposition waterfall chart。\n        Bar 1: Raw formal WR = 66.4%。\n        Bar 2: −3.3% (original preference, green downward)。\n        Bar 3: Net formality causal effect = 63.1% (blue, 13.1% above 50% baseline)。\n        Error bars on final bar from bootstrap CI。\n        Visual proof that formality effect survives original preference correction。\n    analysis: >\n      logistic_formality_coef_p = 0.006 在 [0.001, 0.05] 范围内。Interaction p = 0.58\n      明确不显著。C4 (practical guidance) 有了统计基础：CSD-adjusted win rate 公式为\n      adjusted_wr = raw_wr - β₁/(β₀+β₁) × (raw_wr - 0.50)。这比 ad-hoc additive correction\n      更有统计根据。Paper 可以给出 practitioner checklist：(1) use pairwise over Likert for\n      style bias audit; (2) run RATE control to quantify original preference; (3) report both\n      raw and CSD-adjusted win rates; (4) verify content preservation per axis before applying CSD。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c6d18026-a2ac-4168-b144-93c83fdba8b2","total_cost_usd":1.6164396500000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":46075,"cache_read_input_tokens":223157,"output_tokens":41255,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":46075,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":32770,"cache_read_input_tokens":39080,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18836,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18836},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":8275,"outputTokens":4140,"cacheReadInputTokens":518824,"cacheCreationInputTokens":83696,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.18547739999999996,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":8,"outputTokens":41255,"cacheReadInputTokens":223157,"cacheCreationInputTokens":46075,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.43096225,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"513c3ea1-5240-4162-82ba-2b28b3a7b617"}
